BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ars-electronica-u19-create-your-world-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270303
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270304
SUMMARY:Deadline: Prix Ars Electronica: u19 create your world 2027 (Austria
 \, under 20)
DESCRIPTION:u19 create your world is the youth category of the Prix Ars Ele
 ctronica\, for young people in Austria working with digital media\, techno
 logy\, games\, code\, film\, music\, art and design. Individuals\, project
  groups and school projects may enter. There are two categories: Young Cre
 atives (up to 14\, judged in u10\, u12 and u14 age groups) and Young Profe
 ssionals (14 to 19)\, whose Golden Nica carries EUR 3\,000. ELIGIBILITY: e
 ntrants must be no older than 19 and live in Austria at the submission dea
 dline. Submissions are open now through the online database at calls.ars.e
 lectronica.art/2027/u19/ until 3 March 2027.\n\nOrganisation: Ars Electron
 ica (Prix Ars Electronica)\nLocation: Linz\, Austria\; open only to people
  aged 19 or younger who live in Austria on 3 March 2027\nAward: Young Prof
 essionals (14 to 19): Golden Nica EUR 3\,000\, two Awards of Distinction E
 UR 800 each\, ten Honorary Mentions. Young Creatives (up to 14): per age g
 roup (u10\, u12\, u14) one EUR 500 Prize plus an Award of Distinction (EUR
  150 for u14\, EUR 100 for u12 and u10). No entry fee mentioned.\nDuration
 : One-off prize\n\nMore: https://ars.electronica.art/createyourworld/en/pr
 ix/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://ars.electronica.art/createyourworld/en/prix/?utm_source=artific
 ialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Linz\, Austria\; open only to people aged 19 or younger who live i
 n Austria on 3 March 2027
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ecf-erasmus-40-creative-research-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261202
SUMMARY:Deadline: European Cultural Foundation: ERASMUS 40 Creative Researc
 h Fellowship (Florence archives\, Brussels presentation)
DESCRIPTION:To mark the 40th anniversary of ERASMUS in 2027\, the European 
 Cultural Foundation is opening its historical archives for a Creative Rese
 arch Fellowship: one professional creative practitioner will research ECF'
 s lesser-known role in shaping the ERASMUS student mobility programme (fro
 m the European Institute of Education and the Office for Cooperation in Ed
 ucation to the ERASMUS Bureau\, which ran the scheme until 1994) and trans
 late that history into a public-facing artwork about what European belongi
 ng feels like and what the next ERASMUS could be. WHAT YOU GET: a EUR 10\,
 000 grant for travel\, living costs and production\; a research residency 
 at the Historical Archives of the European Union in Florence during the fi
 rst trimester of 2027\; and presentation of the finished work in Brussels 
 in September 2027\, in partnership with the House of European History. WHO
 : creative practitioners residing in a Council of Europe member state with
  a track record of research-based work for museum contexts. DEADLINE: 1 De
 cember 2026\, 17:00 CET. The full call is linked from ECF's open calls and
  social channels\; a dedicated call page could not be located at the time 
 of adding.\n\nOrganisation: European Cultural Foundation (ECF)\, with the 
 Historical Archives of the European Union (EUI) and the House of European 
 History\nLocation: Research stay in Florence\, Italy (Historical Archives 
 of the EU) in the first trimester of 2027\; final work presented in Brusse
 ls in September 2027. Open to creative practitioners residing in a Council
  of Europe member state.\nAward: EUR 10\,000 grant covering travel\, livin
 g expenses and artistic production. One fellowship.\nDuration: Research re
 sidency in Florence in the first trimester of 2027 (January to March)\; pr
 esentation in September 2027\n\nMore: https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-c
 alls/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-calls/?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Research stay in Florence\, Italy (Historical Archives of the EU) 
 in the first trimester of 2027\; final work presented in Brussels in Septe
 mber 2027. Open to creative practitioners residing in a Council of Europe 
 member state.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:casa-de-velazquez-artists-in-residence-2027-2028@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261127
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261128
SUMMARY:Deadline: Casa de Velazquez: Artists in Residence 2027-2028 (Academ
 ie de France a Madrid)
DESCRIPTION:The Academie de France a Madrid at the Casa de Velazquez offers
  12 one-year residencies for 2027-2028 to young graduates and established 
 artists developing a creative project in the Iberian Peninsula. Applicants
  declare one main discipline: drawing\, printmaking\, sculpture\, painting
 \, architecture\, music composition\, choreography\, photography\, or film
  and video (multidisciplinary development during the year is welcome). REQ
 UIREMENTS: over 18\; a higher arts diploma or a body of work judged by the
  committee\; good French (application and interview in French)\; individua
 l applications only (no collectives)\; at most three applications per life
 time. STATUS: EU/Schengen nationals must show affiliation to an artist/aut
 hor or self-employed scheme\; non-EU applicants need a French residence pe
 rmit allowing work (to join URSSAF artists/authors) or a Schengen residenc
 e and work permit from another EU state plus artist-author status there\, 
 covering the whole residency. APPLICATION: online portal with a project of
  up to 5\,000 characters in French\, expectations and career fit (600 char
 acters each)\, CV in French (max 3 pages)\, portfolio (A3 landscape PDF\, 
 max 10 pages)\, up to two video links of max 10 minutes\, audio files (com
 posers must include a chamber or orchestral work with score)\, up to 10 ph
 otos and up to two recommendation letters. SELECTION: pre-selection the we
 ek of 8 March 2027\, interviews in French in Paris the week of 5 April 202
 7\, results mid-April 2027. Residents must live at the Casa outside closur
 e periods and take part in its exhibitions and concerts. DEADLINE: 27 Nove
 mber 2026\, 13:00 Madrid time. Questions: candidatures-cvz@casadevelazquez
 .org.\n\nOrganisation: Casa de Velazquez\, Academie de France a Madrid\nLo
 cation: Madrid\, Spain (residence at the Casa de Velazquez). No nationalit
 y requirement\, but EU/Schengen nationals must be affiliated to an artist/
 author or self-employed scheme in their country of residence\, and non-EU 
 applicants need a French residence permit allowing work or a Schengen work
  and residence permit from another EU state. Good French required.\nAward:
  Monthly residency grant voted each year\; for 2026-2027 it was EUR 3\,600
  per month for artists housed at the Casa and EUR 4\,600 per month for art
 ists living outside (with children). Twelve monthly payments\, September 2
 027 to August 2028. Housing and studio provided\; a production support fun
 d is also available on project. No application fee.\nDuration: 12 months (
 1 September 2027 to 31 August 2028\; on site mid-September to about 20 Jul
 y)\n\nMore: https://www.casadevelazquez.org/que-pasa-en-la-casa/detail/app
 el-artistes-en-residence-2027-2028?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.casadevelazquez.org/que-pasa-en-la-casa/detail/appel-artist
 es-en-residence-2027-2028?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium
 =referral
LOCATION:Madrid\, Spain (residence at the Casa de Velazquez). No nationalit
 y requirement\, but EU/Schengen nationals must be affiliated to an artist/
 author or self-employed scheme in their country of residence\, and non-EU 
 applicants need a French residence permit allowing work or a Schengen work
  and residence permit from another EU state. Good French required.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai-horizons-parma-360-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Deadline: AI Horizons: Art Beyond Algorithms (PARMA 360 Festival\, 
 Parma European Youth Capital 2027)
DESCRIPTION:First edition of an international call for artists under 35 wor
 king with artificial intelligence\, digital languages and emerging technol
 ogies\, run by 360° Creativity Events APS for PARMA 360 Festival and Parm
 a European Youth Capital 2027. It follows the 2026 pilot exhibition SYNTHE
 TIC HORIZONS (curated by Chiara Canali). The call focuses on open-source a
 nd closed-source image and video generation tools and their creative\, soc
 ial and cultural impact. THEMES: Parma Heritage (crafts\, traditions\, arc
 hives\, immersive storytelling of the city)\; La Cura / Care (wellbeing\, 
 accessibility\, AI ethics\, health tech\, public space)\; Sustainability a
 nd Data Ecology (energy and water cost of AI\, data extraction and digital
  colonialism\, waste of digital images\, ethics of automated production). 
 ACCEPTED FORMATS: digital and synthetic images\, NFTs\, printed digital ph
 otography\, digital/3D-printed sculpture\, video\, audio\, interactive bro
 wser or chatbot installations\, software art\, VR\, AR\, sound art\, perfo
 rmance and hybrids. Works must already be completed but need not be unpubl
 ished. One application per artist. REQUIRED: an Artist Statement (max 1\,5
 00 characters) on how you use AI\, naming software\, models and workflow\;
  missing statements are excluded. SELECTION: a jury of the PARMA 360 artis
 tic direction\, the Parma EYC27 committee and AI/new-tech experts picks 20
  finalists (at least 3 from the Parma area)\, announced from 1 December 20
 26\; finalists show in a group exhibition curated by Chiara Canali in Parm
 a in April-May 2027. The organiser covers shipping to the show and AV equi
 pment hire and gives finalists one hotel night at the opening\; return shi
 pping and travel are at the artist's cost. Prize-winning works are acquire
 d in full or in part. AGE: must not have turned 35 by the closing date. DE
 ADLINE: 31 October 2026\, midnight Rome time\, via the Google Form linked 
 in the call. Questions: aihorizonscall@gmail.com.\n\nOrganisation: 360° C
 reativity Events APS (PARMA 360 Festival della creatività contemporanea)\
 , with Parma European Youth Capital 2027\nLocation: Parma\, Italy. Open to
  Italian and international artists under 35 and students of the Accademie 
 di Belle Arti. Finalists exhibit in Parma in April-May 2027.\nAward: EUR 6
 \,000 in cash prizes (gross): 1st AI Horizons Prize EUR 1\,500 (overall wi
 nner) plus three sponsor prizes of EUR 1\,500 each (Polo Parma for Parma H
 eritage\, COLSER-Auroradomus for La Cura\, DS Solutions for Sustainability
  and Data Ecology). The top prize can be combined with a sponsor prize\, s
 o one artist can receive up to EUR 3\,000. Prizes are treated as full or p
 artial acquisition of the work. Non-cash: Piazza of Beauty residency in Pa
 rma during the show\, plus Rome New Media Week 2027 and Premio Giovanarte 
 exhibition mentions. Free to enter.\nDuration: Finalist group exhibition i
 n April-May 2027 (11th PARMA 360 Festival)\n\nMore: https://forms.gle/ymoW
 bcjuDyzJY11P6?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://forms.gle/ymoWbcjuDyzJY11P6?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Parma\, Italy. Open to Italian and international artists under 35 
 and students of the Accademie di Belle Arti. Finalists exhibit in Parma in
  April-May 2027.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:athens-digital-arts-festival-2027-open-call@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261110
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261111
SUMMARY:Deadline: Athens Digital Arts Festival 2027 (23rd edition): Open Ca
 ll "It's Alive..."
DESCRIPTION:The Athens Digital Arts Festival\, Greece's long-running digita
 l arts festival\, has opened its call for the 23rd edition in spring 2027 
 under the theme "It's Alive..." (Dr. Frankenstein's line\, reread for an a
 ge when we feel the same relief when the Wi-Fi comes back). CATEGORIES: Vi
 deo Art\, Installations\, Performances\, Animation\, Games\, Web Art\, AR/
 VR/XR\, Music\, Talks\, Workshops and ADAF Kids. Up to 4 entries per categ
 ory\, one form per work\; digital-image collections of up to 5 works can s
 hare one application. Videos max 30 minutes (online file up to 2 GB in .av
 i\, .mpeg or .mov\, or a Vimeo link). Unrealised works with a complete con
 cept and design are eligible if they can be ready about two months before 
 the festival. Curators share applications across categories\, so a work ma
 y be accepted in a different one. Shortlisted artists are contacted by ema
 il\; others are not notified. NO ENTRY FEE. No artist fee or prize is publ
 ished. DEADLINE: 10 November 2026\, via the forms at 2027.adaf.gr. Questio
 ns: info@adaf.gr.\n\nOrganisation: Athens Digital Arts Festival (ADAF)\nLo
 cation: Athens\, Greece (23rd edition\, spring 2027). Open to artists\, re
 searchers\, thinkers and organisations worldwide.\nAward: NO PUBLISHED CAS
 H\, listed under the desk's festival exception (festival calls with a firm
  deadline may be added without a cash amount). No entry fee. Postal submis
 sion costs and artwork transport are at the artist's expense unless agreed
  otherwise.\n\nMore: https://2027.adaf.gr/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://2027.adaf.gr/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=
 referral
LOCATION:Athens\, Greece (23rd edition\, spring 2027). Open to artists\, re
 searchers\, thinkers and organisations worldwide.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:thessaloniki-documentary-festival-agora-xr-lab-2027@artificialnouveau.g
 ithub.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261125
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261126
SUMMARY:Deadline: Thessaloniki Documentary Festival: AGORA XR Lab 2027 (XR 
 and new media projects in development)
DESCRIPTION:A development lab for XR and new media projects at the Thessalo
 niki International Documentary Festival's industry section AGORA\, for eme
 rging storytellers working across film\, digital media\, new technologies 
 and performing arts. Lead mentor: Vassiliki Khonsari (co-founder\, iNK Sto
 ries). Up to five projects are selected. FORMAT: online preparation and pr
 oject-enhancement workshop in mid-January 2027\, then the lab in Thessalon
 iki on 6-11 March 2027 with industry meetings scheduled from professionals
 ' requests and the AGORA team\, plus online meetings on 12 March. ELIGIBIL
 ITY: teams of at least two creative members (creator-creator or creator-pr
 oducer)\, any development stage\; one lead can submit up to two projects\;
  previously rejected projects only with substantial changes. Both core mem
 bers must attend the January workshop and at least one must attend the ful
 l lab. Completed projects must credit the lab. APPLICATION: English online
  form (not editable after submission) plus one English PDF with logline\, 
 synopsis (max 2 pages)\, format and audience thoughts\, team bios\, financ
 ing plan if available\, visual material and past work. Notification early 
 January 2027. DEADLINE: 25 November 2026. Contact: Rafaela Karagianni.\n\n
 Organisation: Thessaloniki International Documentary Festival (TIDF AGORA)
 \nLocation: Thessaloniki\, Greece (online workshop mid-January 2027\, in-p
 erson lab 6-11 March 2027). Aimed at projects produced or co-produced in\,
  or with story links to\, Southeast and Central Europe\, the Mediterranean
  and parts of the Middle East and North Africa\; projects from elsewhere m
 ay still apply.\nAward: NO CASH\, listed under the desk's festival excepti
 on (festival calls with a firm deadline may be added without a cash amount
 ). Selected projects get 5 nights' accommodation (one double room for two 
 members)\, partial travel reimbursement against receipts\, mentoring and c
 urated industry meetings. No application fee stated.\nDuration: Online wor
 kshop mid-January 2027\, in-person lab 6-11 March 2027\n\nMore: https://fi
 lmfestival.gr/en/tidf/tidf-agora/agora-xr-lab/?utm_source=artificialnouvea
 ugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://filmfestival.gr/en/tidf/tidf-agora/agora-xr-lab/?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Thessaloniki\, Greece (online workshop mid-January 2027\, in-perso
 n lab 6-11 March 2027). Aimed at projects produced or co-produced in\, or 
 with story links to\, Southeast and Central Europe\, the Mediterranean and
  parts of the Middle East and North Africa\; projects from elsewhere may s
 till apply.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quindici-minuti-di-riflessione-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261130
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261201
SUMMARY:Deadline: Quindici Minuti di Riflessione 2027: Short Performance Co
 mpetition (1st edition\, Sassari)
DESCRIPTION:First edition of an international competition for short live pe
 rformances of around fifteen minutes in dance and physical theatre\, run b
 y Music & Movie ETS within the InterAgendo project. Works must carry an et
 hical\, civic or social theme. Six companies are selected to perform in Sa
 ssari on 6-8 May 2027 in front of a National Jury\, a Schools and Communit
 y Jury and a Territorial Jury. MONEY: each selected company receives a gua
 ranteed gross fee of EUR 500 (solo)\, EUR 700 (duo) or EUR 900 (three or m
 ore performers) plus three nights' accommodation\; the Best Work Award is 
 EUR 1\,000 and the Reflections Award EUR 400. Application is free\; only t
 he six selected companies pay a EUR 50 security deposit\, refunded in full
  at the end of the festival. Similar in format to Teatri Riflessi in Sicil
 y. DEADLINE: 30 November 2026\, 23:59 CET.\n\nOrganisation: Music & Movie 
 ETS (InterAgendo project)\nLocation: Sala Teatrale Palazzo di Città\, Sas
 sari\, Sardinia\, Italy (6-8 May 2027). Open to Italian and international 
 companies and artists.\nAward: Guaranteed gross all-inclusive fee for each
  of six selected companies: EUR 500 (solo)\, EUR 700 (duo)\, EUR 900 (thre
 e or more performers)\, plus three nights' accommodation. Prizes: Best Wor
 k Award EUR 1\,000 gross (National Jury) and Reflections Award EUR 400 gro
 ss for the work with the strongest ethical and civic impact (Schools and C
 ommunity Jury and Territorial Jury). Free to apply\; selected companies pa
 y a EUR 50 deposit\, fully refunded after the festival.\nDuration: Festiva
 l 6-8 May 2027\n\nMore: https://musicandmovie.art/quindici-minuti-di-rifle
 ssione-concorso-internazionale-di-spettacoli-brevi/?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://musicandmovie.art/quindici-minuti-di-riflessione-concorso-inter
 nazionale-di-spettacoli-brevi/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_m
 edium=referral
LOCATION:Sala Teatrale Palazzo di Città\, Sassari\, Sardinia\, Italy (6-8 
 May 2027). Open to Italian and international companies and artists.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:graner-creative-grants-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260929
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260930
SUMMARY:Deadline: Graner Creative Grants 2027: Residencies for Dance and Li
 ve Arts (Barcelona)
DESCRIPTION:Graner\, Barcelona's centre for dance and live arts creation wi
 thin the city council's Creative Factories Network\, managed by Mercat de 
 les Flors with the Catalan dance professionals' associations APDC and ACPD
 C\, opens its 2027 call for residency grants supporting creation and resea
 rch projects taking place between January and December 2027. EIGHT CATEGOR
 IES: Associated Artist (1 place\, EUR 6\,000 per year for 2027 and 2028\, 
 for Catalonia-based artists who associate with the centre for two years\, 
 with a creative residency of up to six weeks)\; Creation (3 places\, EUR 6
 \,000\, local and national artists developing projects leading to a produc
 tion\, up to five weeks)\; Barcelona Crea Research (2 places\, EUR 6\,000\
 , local researchers and artists in the initial stages of artistic research
  with body\, movement and choreographic thinking as its axes)\; Barcelona 
 Crea Critical Thinking (1 place\, EUR 6\,000\, theoretical\, critical or d
 iscursive projects on dance and the live arts)\; International (1 place\, 
 EUR 3\,000\, for researchers\, artists and collectives based outside Spain
  without a direct connection to the Catalan or Spanish context\, two to fo
 ur weeks\; applying here excludes all other categories)\; Stage Research (
 1 place\, EUR 3\,000\, research centred on lighting\, sound\, video or sce
 nography\, with technical studio time and support sessions)\; Emerging Art
 ists (2 places\, EUR 3\,000\, endowment topped up with EUR 1\,700 contribu
 ted by Can Gassol in Mataro\, where part of the residency takes place)\; a
 nd Practical Methodologies (1 place\, EUR 3\,000). WHAT YOU GET: on top of
  the grant\, a workspace agreed per project\, possible technical residency
 \, shared desk and facilities\, artistic support and possible specialised 
 mentoring\, participation in Graner's labs\, workshops and seminars\, comm
 unication support\, and covered national and European travel to the two an
 nual APLEC gatherings. ELIGIBILITY: natural persons\, legal persons and gr
 oups with or without legal personality\; applicants may apply to at most t
 wo categories (International is mutually exclusive) and can receive only o
 ne grant. Barcelona Crea categories require a demonstrated connection to B
 arcelona or its metropolitan area and carry municipal-grant incompatibilit
 y rules. NOTE: structural renovation works run at Graner throughout 2027 a
 nd may affect studio use. APPLICATION: free\, via the category-specific fo
 rms on the Mercat de les Flors website\; an English-language bases PDF det
 ails each category. DEADLINE: 29 September 2026 at 14:00 Catalan time (12:
 00 UTC).\n\nOrganisation: El Graner Fabrica de Creacio\, managed by Mercat
  de les Flors\nLocation: Graner\, Barcelona\, Spain (with part of the Emer
 ging Artists residencies at Can Gassol\, Mataro). Most categories are for 
 local and national artists\; one International category is reserved for ar
 tists based outside Spain.\nAward: 12 grants totalling EUR 57\,000. EUR 6\
 ,000 per project for Associated Artist (1 place\, EUR 6\,000 each for 2027
  and 2028)\, Creation (3 places)\, Barcelona Crea Research (2) and Barcelo
 na Crea Critical Thinking (1). EUR 3\,000 per project for Stage Research (
 1)\, International (1)\, Emerging Artists (2\, endowment topped up with EU
 R 1\,700 from Can Gassol) and Practical Methodologies (1). Plus workspace\
 , possible technical residency\, artistic support and covered travel to th
 e two annual APLEC gatherings. No application fee.\nDuration: Residencies 
 between January and December 2027\, typically up to four to six weeks\, no
 t necessarily consecutive\, depending on category. The Associated Artist c
 ommits for two years (2027-2028).\n\nMore: https://mercatflors.cat/en/beca
 /2027-call-for-proposals-for-creative-grants-el-graner-fabrica-de-creacio/
 ?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://mercatflors.cat/en/beca/2027-call-for-proposals-for-creative-gr
 ants-el-graner-fabrica-de-creacio/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Graner\, Barcelona\, Spain (with part of the Emerging Artists resi
 dencies at Can Gassol\, Mataro). Most categories are for local and nationa
 l artists\; one International category is reserved for artists based outsi
 de Spain.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:supporting-act-foundation-artist-grant-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Deadline: The Supporting Act Foundation: Artist Grant 2026
DESCRIPTION:The Supporting Act Foundation\, the charitable foundation estab
 lished by WeTransfer\, awards ten unrestricted Artist Grants of EUR 10\,00
 0 to emerging artists from underrepresented groups whose work involves col
 laborative\, collective or creative processes that benefit their communiti
 es. The grant is paid as EUR 1\,000 per month over one year and can be use
 d freely\; applicants should explain how it would help them overcome econo
 mic\, social\, cultural\, physical or health barriers to their practice. E
 LIGIBILITY: identify as an emerging artist with at least two and no more t
 han ten years of professional experience\; identify as belonging to an und
 errepresented group or face systemic barriers to your career\; be born in 
 or before 2005\; be based in Belgium\, France\, Germany\, Greece\, Ireland
 \, Italy\, the Netherlands\, Portugal\, Spain or the United Kingdom with a
  personal IBAN bank account there\; and have an updated website or public 
 social media profile. Former and current TSAF grantees cannot apply. TIMEL
 INE: applications close 1 October 2026 at 11:00 CET\, notifications go to 
 all applicants in late October 2026\, shortlisted applicants get a final r
 eview in November 2026\, and the public announcement and first transfer fo
 llow in January 2027. APPLICATION: free\, via the open call platform on th
 e foundation's website. The parallel Impact Grant strand for arts nonprofi
 ts runs on the same deadline.\n\nOrganisation: The Supporting Act Foundati
 on\nLocation: Remote\; for artists based in Belgium\, France\, Germany\, G
 reece\, Ireland\, Italy\, the Netherlands\, Portugal\, Spain or the United
  Kingdom.\nAward: 10 unrestricted grants of EUR 10\,000 each\, paid out at
  EUR 1\,000 per month over one year\, with the first installment transferr
 ed in January 2027. No application fee.\nDuration: One year\, from January
  2027.\n\nMore: https://thesupportingact.org/programs/artist-grant/2026?ut
 m_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://thesupportingact.org/programs/artist-grant/2026?utm_source=arti
 ficialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote\; for artists based in Belgium\, France\, Germany\, Greece\
 , Ireland\, Italy\, the Netherlands\, Portugal\, Spain or the United Kingd
 om.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:supporting-act-foundation-impact-grant-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Deadline: The Supporting Act Foundation: Impact Grant 2026 for Arts
  Nonprofits
DESCRIPTION:The Supporting Act Foundation\, the charitable foundation estab
 lished by WeTransfer\, awards ten unrestricted Impact Grants of EUR 50\,00
 0 (EUR 25\,000 per year over two years) to arts-focused nonprofits that em
 power emerging artists from underrepresented groups through non-financial 
 support: improving artists' living conditions\, enabling practice developm
 ent\, increasing the visibility of their work and building their confidenc
 e. ELIGIBILITY: nonprofits registered as arts organizations between 2016 a
 nd 2024\, based in Belgium\, France\, Germany\, Greece\, Ireland\, Italy\,
  the Netherlands\, Portugal\, Spain or the United Kingdom\, or working wit
 h a fiscal host in one of these countries\; annual expenditures between EU
 R 50\,000 and EUR 300\,000\; an active website demonstrating supported pro
 jects\; and an IBAN bank account. Individuals\, commercial entities\, curr
 ent or past TSAF grantees\, and proposals for ongoing projects rather than
  established organizations are not eligible. TIMELINE: applications close 
 1 October 2026 at 11:00 CET\, are reviewed in October\, notifications go o
 ut in late October 2026\, shortlisted organizations get a final review in 
 November 2026\, and the public announcement and first installment follow i
 n January 2027. APPLICATION: free\, via the open call platform on the foun
 dation's website. The parallel Artist Grant strand for individual emerging
  artists runs on the same deadline.\n\nOrganisation: The Supporting Act Fo
 undation\nLocation: Remote\; for nonprofits registered in Belgium\, France
 \, Germany\, Greece\, Ireland\, Italy\, the Netherlands\, Portugal\, Spain
  or the United Kingdom\, or working with a fiscal host there.\nAward: 10 u
 nrestricted grants of EUR 50\,000 each\, paid as EUR 25\,000 per year over
  two years\, with the first transfer in January 2027. No application fee.\
 nDuration: Two years\, from January 2027.\n\nMore: https://thesupportingac
 t.org/programs/impact-grant/2026?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm
 _medium=referral
