UID:rtm-pitch-iffr-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260830
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260831
SUMMARY:Deadline: RTM Pitch 2026 (IFFR)
DESCRIPTION:Eighth edition of RTM Pitch\, IFFR's open call for Rotterdam fi
 lm talent. Submit a plan for a film between 5 and 20 minutes long\; a jury
  of film experts and IFFR programmers selects one filmmaker to receive EUR
  25\,000 to realise the film (with coaching and an IFFR 2028 premiere) and
  a runner-up to receive a EUR 5\,000 development budget co-funded by QISSA
 . All filmmakers are welcome\; this edition especially encourages genre fi
 lms (horror\, science fiction\, thriller\, fantasy) that use genre convent
 ions for a distinctive personal vision. Submit a written film plan (story\
 , setting\, team\, budget and financing\, cinematography vision\, with opt
 ional supporting material) or a video pitch of no more than three minutes 
 (Vimeo or YouTube link) via the application form. Deadline: Sunday 30 Augu
 st 2026\, 23:59 CEST.\n\nOrganisation: International Film Festival Rotterd
 am (IFFR)\nLocation: Rotterdam\, Netherlands\nAward: EUR 25\,000 for the w
 inner (EUR 20\,000 from the City of Rotterdam\, EUR 5\,000 from VEVAM Fond
 s) to realise the film\, plus tailored coaching and an IFFR premiere\; a r
 unner-up receives a EUR 5\,000 development budget co-funded by QISSA. No a
 pplication fee.\nDuration: Short film of 5 to 20 minutes\; winning film pr
 emieres during RTM Day at IFFR 2028\n\nMore: https://iffr.com/en/blog-rtm-
 pitch?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://iffr.com/en/blog-rtm-pitch?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Rotterdam\, Netherlands
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:transmediale-pro-helvetia-digital-art-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.
 github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260829
SUMMARY:Deadline: transmediale x Pro Helvetia Digital Art Residency 2027
DESCRIPTION:The fifth iteration of transmediale's Digital Art Residency\, r
 un with the Swiss Arts Council Pro Helvetia\, awarded to one individual or
  collective working in digital art practices at the intersection of media 
 arts\, performance\, sound and moving image. THEME: the 2027 programme sit
 s under transmediale's 40th-anniversary framework RFC 40\, named after the
  early internet Request for Comments series\, and treats the festival as a
  counter-infrastructure: the call asks how a network stays legible to itse
 lf while surrounding structures break down\, and how technical paradigms c
 an be reconfigured into new cultural protocols outside extractive logics\,
  moving from critique to construction. Proposals should offer alternatives
  to how we understand\, respond to and shape the technological conditions 
 we inhabit. WHAT IS OFFERED: an artist fee of CHF 2\,000 per month for two
  months\; a CHF 15\,000 production grant supporting a new work or the cont
 inuation of an existing project\, open to all formats and building on the 
 research begun during the residency (the project must be completed by Dece
 mber 2027 at the latest)\; travel and accommodation for the festival and t
 he residency\; a shared modular working space at transmediale studio\; con
 nections to Berlin institutions and stakeholders\; a public presentation i
 n transmediale's year-round studio programme\; and the option of an online
  publication in transmediale's journal. STRUCTURE: kick-off with a present
 ation of the residency projects during transmediale 2027 (26 to 31 January
  2027\, attendance optional but strongly recommended)\; onboarding and the
  first hybrid stretch in May 2027\; the mandatory on-site month in Berlin 
 in June 2027\; and a second hybrid stretch including reporting in July 202
 7. Availability for the festival week and for the whole of June in Berlin 
 are treated as key prerequisites. TIMELINE: open call 16 July to 28 August
  2026 (23:59 CEST)\; selected residents announced October 2026. Applicatio
 ns are only accepted via transmediale's submission forms. Contact: info[at
 ]transmediale.de.\n\nOrganisation: transmediale (in cooperation with the S
 wiss Arts Council Pro Helvetia)\nLocation: Hybrid: remote plus on-site at 
 transmediale studio\, silent green Kulturquartier\, Berlin-Wedding\, Germa
 ny. RESTRICTED: applicants must hold Swiss nationality or permanent reside
 nce in Switzerland and be firmly established in the Swiss cultural scene (
 Pro Helvetia's general requirements apply).\nAward: Artist fee of CHF 2\,0
 00 per month across the two-month residency (CHF 4\,000)\, plus a producti
 on grant of CHF 15\,000 for the selected project\, plus travel and accommo
 dation for both the festival and the residency month. Duos and collectives
  may apply but the fee and the production grant stay the same and must be 
 shared. No application fee.\nDuration: Two-month hybrid residency between 
 mid-May and mid-July 2027\, with the whole of June 2027 on-site in Berlin 
 (mandatory)\n\nMore: https://transmediale.de/en/news/digital-art-residency
 -2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://transmediale.de/en/news/digital-art-residency-2027?utm_source=a
 rtificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Hybrid: remote plus on-site at transmediale studio\, silent green 
 Kulturquartier\, Berlin-Wedding\, Germany. RESTRICTED: applicants must hol
 d Swiss nationality or permanent residence in Switzerland and be firmly es
 tablished in the Swiss cultural scene (Pro Helvetia's general requirements
  apply).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:klang-copenhagen-open-call-2027-music-movement@artificialnouveau.github
 .io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Klang Copenhagen Avantgarde Music Festival: Open Call 202
 7\, MUSIC/MOVEMENT
DESCRIPTION:Klang\, Copenhagen's avantgarde music festival\, is seeking one
  to three projects at the intersection of experimental music and movement\
 , dance or choreography for its 2027 edition at Dansehallerne. Important c
 onstraint: the call is explicitly for ready-to-go projects\, not commissio
 ns or works in progress\, so the work must already be finished and product
 ion-ready. Submission is a one-page PDF covering artistic description\, bu
 dget overview\, bios\, duration and media links\, emailed to opencall@klan
 g.dk with 'Open Call 2027' in the subject line. The submission window runs
  1 July to 1 September 2026. The toaspern|moeller duo together with Klang 
 Festival review feasible submissions in September 2026\, with notification
  in October 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Klang - Copenhagen Avantgarde Music Fes
 tival\nLocation: Dansehallerne\, Copenhagen\, Denmark. No nationality\, ag
 e or education restrictions are stated on the call page.\nAward: Klang aim
 s to cover production costs and performer fees. Travel and accommodation a
 re discussed case by case rather than guaranteed. No commission fee is off
 ered\, since the call seeks finished work rather than new creation. No app
 lication fee.\nDuration: Performance during Klang Festival 2027\, provisio
 nal dates 15 to 18 June 2027\n\nMore: https://www.klang.dk/open-calls/open
 call2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.klang.dk/open-calls/opencall2027?utm_source=artificialnouve
 augrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Dansehallerne\, Copenhagen\, Denmark. No nationality\, age or educ
 ation restrictions are stated on the call page.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:waag-trust-me-im-an-airtist-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: Trust me\, I'm an AI/rtist: Open Call for Creative Interv
 entions
DESCRIPTION:Waag Futurelab invites artists\, theatre makers\, choreographer
 s\, dancers\, game designers and other creative practitioners to engage di
 rectly with seven experimental generative AI Enablers being co-created wit
 h technologists and dance\, theatre and gaming professionals. The call is 
 an invitation into the development process: selected artists get access to
  the technologies\, datasets\, interfaces and assumptions that shape these
  systems while they are still being built. Rather than testing whether the
  systems work\, artists are asked to interrogate why they work the way the
 y do\, who they are designed for\, what forms of creativity they enable or
  constrain\, and what assumptions about culture\, intelligence\, authorshi
 p\, labour\, bodies\, audiences and society are embedded in them. Waag is 
 looking for individuals and collectives willing to move beyond adoption in
 to investigation\, and welcomes proposals that are speculative\, critical\
 , poetic\, provocative\, humorous\, performative\, constructive or disrupt
 ive\, including work that challenges\, misuses\, reimagines\, hacks\, subv
 erts or plays with the tools\, exposes hidden biases\, questions environme
 ntal costs\, or imagines alternative technological futures. THE SEVEN AI E
 NABLERS\, each requiring an on-site visit to its technology partner: the G
 eneric Procedural Content Generation Enabler (text-to-3D assets and avatar
 s\, CERTH\, Greece)\; the Data-Driven Cultural Content Adaptation Enabler 
 (audience-aware creative content ideation with ranked candidate ideas\, CE
 RTH\, Greece)\; the Cross-Domain Audience Engagement Analytics Enabler (tu
 rning heterogeneous cultural participation data into interpretable engagem
 ent signals\, The Audience Agency\, Warrington\, UK)\; the Dance Style Ana
 lysis and Generation Enabler (dance video into virtual 3D choreography\, d
 issected into body\, effort\, shape and space components\, Centre of Excel
 lence for Research & Innovation\, Cyprus)\; the Immersive Design Integrati
 on Enabler for Dance & Theatre (NLP-driven XR environments with speech-to-
 3D scene editing\, Cyprus)\; the Music-to-Movement Translation Enabler (au
 dio into a time-aligned feature set spanning genre classification\, emotio
 nal valence-arousal analysis\, rhythm extraction and latent-space projecti
 on\, feeding motion generation\, spatial audio and visual choreography\, A
 ristotle University of Thessaloniki\, Greece)\; and the Adaptive Narrative
  Enabler for Games & Theatre (an evolutionary AI trained on creator-writte
 n story elements that generates infinite story variations\, explicitly rej
 ecting LLMs because of their dependence on copyrighted or public-domain co
 rpora that encode 19th and early 20th century sexism\, racism and imperial
 ism\, CAUSA Creation\, Austria). ELIGIBILITY: artists\, designers\, creati
 ve technologists\, theatre makers\, dancers\, choreographers and game desi
 gners\, as individuals or collectives\; applicants must hold a European VA
 T number. An info session with live demonstrations of the AI Enablers runs
  31 July 2026\, 10:00 to 11:30 CEST (meeting ID 995 7016 2341). Applicatio
 ns go through Homerun using the official Application Template\, uploaded a
 s a PDF\; read the Guide for Applicants\, which contains the full Enabler 
 descriptions\, before applying. Questions: zoenie at waag dot org. The AI 
 Enablers and this call are part of the Horizon Europe project HAMLET\, whi
 ch aims to make generative AI accessible to cultural organisations of all 
 sizes. Closes 30 September 2026\, 23:59 CEST. Free to apply.\n\nOrganisati
 on: Waag Futurelab (Horizon Europe project HAMLET)\nLocation: Europe. Enga
 ging with a specific AI Enabler includes an on-site visit to its technolog
 y partner: CERTH (Greece)\, The Audience Agency (Warrington\, UK)\, the Ce
 ntre of Excellence for Research & Innovation (Cyprus)\, Aristotle Universi
 ty of Thessaloniki (Greece)\, or CAUSA Creation (Austria). Final presentat
 ions September 2027.\nAward: EUR 20\,000 commission fee excluding VAT\, in
 clusive of artist fee\, travel\, accommodation and production costs. Appli
 cants must have a VAT number in Europe. No application fee.\nDuration: Jan
 uary to September 2027\, with final presentations in September 2027\n\nMor
 e: https://waag.org/en/article/open-call-creative-interventions-trust-me-i
 m-airtist/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://waag.org/en/article/open-call-creative-interventions-trust-me-i
 m-airtist/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Europe. Engaging with a specific AI Enabler includes an on-site vi
 sit to its technology partner: CERTH (Greece)\, The Audience Agency (Warri
 ngton\, UK)\, the Centre of Excellence for Research & Innovation (Cyprus)\
 , Aristotle University of Thessaloniki (Greece)\, or CAUSA Creation (Austr
 ia). Final presentations September 2027.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:drift-choreographer-open-call-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260831
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260901
SUMMARY:Deadline: DRIFT: Choreographer Open Call 2026-27 (Dance and Researc
 h In The Future Time)
DESCRIPTION:DRIFT (Dance and Research In The Future Time) is a four-year Cr
 eative Europe cooperation between ten European organisations\, led by Thea
 tre de Liege and Maison de la danse. The distinguishing feature is that it
  funds artistic research rather than production: you are expected to arriv
 e with questions\, not a finished piece you already intend to make\, and r
 eviewers read every section of the application through that lens. STRUCTUR
 E: each of the ten partner organisations selects one choreographer from it
 s own country\, forming a cohort of ten. Over the programme you get an Onb
 oarding Lab\, two weeks of residency with your national partner\, three co
 llaborative Online Labs\, a Festival Lab in Tunis\, individual artistic an
 d curatorial mentoring\, and a work-in-progress showcase at the Biennale d
 e la danse in Lyon\, all backed by a EUR 20\,000 research budget that cove
 rs your fees\, travel\, accommodation and any collaborators. SECOND PHASE:
  after a further evaluation\, five of the ten artists may receive co-produ
 ction support and touring across the DRIFT network. That phase is separate
  from this application and is not guaranteed. ELIGIBILITY: professional ch
 oreographers in contemporary dance or performance\, at a mid-career stage\
 , meaning an established national practice but not yet fully established i
 nternationally. You must be based in Belgium\, France\, Germany (Berlin re
 gion only)\, Greece\, Norway\, Italy\, Spain\, Ukraine\, Tunisia or Portug
 al\, and you apply through the partner organisation representing your coun
 try of residence\, not centrally. Good English and availability for all pr
 ogramme dates are required. The country list is strict\, so check it befor
 e you start. TIMELINE: applications opened 1 July 2026 and close 31 August
  2026\; selection through September\; results 9 October 2026\; programme r
 uns November 2026 to September 2027.\n\nOrganisation: DRIFT\, a four-year 
 Creative Europe cooperation of ten organisations led by Theatre de Liege a
 nd Maison de la danse\nLocation: Activities across Europe: kick-off in Ber
 lin\, Festival Lab in Tunis\, showcase in Lyon\, online labs\, plus a resi
 dency hosted by your own national DRIFT partner. Applicants must be based 
 in Belgium\, France\, Germany (Berlin region only)\, Greece\, Norway\, Ita
 ly\, Spain\, Ukraine\, Tunisia or Portugal\, and apply through the partner
  organisation for their country of residence.\nAward: EUR 20\,000 research
  budget per choreographer\, covering artistic fees\, travel\, accommodatio
 n and optional collaborator costs. Also included: an Onboarding Lab\, two 
 weeks of residency with your national DRIFT partner\, three collaborative 
 Online Labs\, a Festival Lab in Tunis\, individual artistic mentoring and 
 individual curatorial mentoring\, and a work-in-progress presentation at t
 he Biennale de la danse in Lyon. No application fee.\nDuration: November 2
 026 to September 2027. Kick-off in Berlin 30 November to 1 December 2026\;
  Festival Lab in Tunis 18-21 March 2027\; Biennale de la danse showcase in
  Lyon 18-25 September 2027.\n\nMore: https://driftdance.eu/artists/open-ca
 ll?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://driftdance.eu/artists/open-call?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Activities across Europe: kick-off in Berlin\, Festival Lab in Tun
 is\, showcase in Lyon\, online labs\, plus a residency hosted by your own 
 national DRIFT partner. Applicants must be based in Belgium\, France\, Ger
 many (Berlin region only)\, Greece\, Norway\, Italy\, Spain\, Ukraine\, Tu
 nisia or Portugal\, and apply through the partner organisation for their c
 ountry of residence.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:julies-bicycle-iter-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: ITER 2026: International Touring and Environmental Respon
 sibility Programme
DESCRIPTION:ITER is now in its fifth year and supports people in the perfor
 ming arts to build environmentally responsible\, inclusive and equitable w
 ays of touring and collaborating internationally. It is initiated and fina
 nced by Arts Council England\, Arts Council Norway\, Creative Scotland and
  the Danish Arts Foundation\, and designed and delivered by Julie's Bicycl
 e and in futurum. Creative Scotland joined as a partner for 2026. TWO TRAC
 KS\, up to 60 places in total: PATHFINDERS\, ten sessions introducing the 
 principles of sustainable touring for people new to the subject\; and CHAN
 GEMAKERS\, nine sessions for those further along\, on leadership and syste
 mic change. Seminars run weekly from 1 October to 10 December 2026\, Pathf
 inders on Tuesdays and Changemakers on Thursdays\, 10:00 to 12:00 UK time\
 , alongside networking and a new alumni network. THE MONEY COMES IN PHASE 
 TWO: after the seminars\, groups of three or more participants can apply f
 or up to GBP 30\,000 to implement collaborative projects that cut environm
 ental impacts and advance climate justice. Funding applications open 6 Nov
 ember 2026 and close 11 January 2027\; awarded projects begin in spring 20
 27. ELIGIBILITY: based in England\, Scotland\, Norway or Denmark\, working
  in dance\, music or theatre. That covers music and theatre venues receivi
 ng touring work\, festivals\, orchestras\, theatre companies\, solo artist
 s\, performers and musicians\, performing arts producers\, and multidiscip
 linary arts organisations. Applications are made through the relevant nati
 onal funder (Arts Council England open funds\, Creative Scotland targeted 
 funding\, Arts Council Norway\, Danish Arts Foundation). Questions go to e
 nvironmentaltouring@artscouncil.org.uk.\n\nOrganisation: Julie's Bicycle a
 nd in futurum\, funded by Arts Council England\, Arts Council Norway\, Cre
 ative Scotland and the Danish Arts Foundation\nLocation: England\, Scotlan
 d\, Norway and Denmark. Seminars run online.\nAward: The seminar programme
  is free to join. Groups of three or more participants can then apply for 
 up to GBP 30\,000 for collaborative projects\, with funding applications o
 pen 6 November 2026 to 11 January 2027 and projects starting spring 2027. 
 No application fee.\nDuration: Seminars run weekly from 1 October to 10 De
 cember 2026\, Tuesdays for Pathfinders and Thursdays for Changemakers\, 10
 :00 to 12:00 UK time. Deadline to join 1 September 2026.\n\nMore: https://
 juliesbicycle.org/news/iter-2026/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&ut
 m_medium=referral
URL:https://juliesbicycle.org/news/iter-2026/?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:England\, Scotland\, Norway and Denmark. Seminars run online.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:titanik-mcult-residing-non-linear-technologies-sonic-worldings-2027@art
 ificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260830
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260831
SUMMARY:Deadline: Residing Non-linear Technologies and Sonic Worldings (M-C
 ult x Titanik\, Helsinki and Turku)
DESCRIPTION:A new pilot residency from Art and Media Culture Agency M-Cult 
 in Helsinki and Arte artists' association / Titanik gallery in Turku\, sit
 ting at the intersection of art\, media and sonic practice\, funded by the
  Nordic-Baltic Mobility Programme for Culture from Nordic Culture Point. T
 WO ARTISTS will be selected. THE PREMISE: the programme treats technology 
 as a situated practice and deliberately shifts attention away from the pro
 gress narratives promoted by large global technology companies\, toward lo
 cal\, indigenous and community-oriented perspectives. It focuses on making
  vernacular and non-linear technological and sonic environments visible\, 
 foregrounding vibrant local histories and traditions across the Nordic and
  Baltic region\, and asks what non-linear sonic and media practice might l
 ook like in the current social\, political and cultural landscape. WHAT EA
 CH ARTIST RECEIVES: EUR 3\,500 artist fee\; EUR 2\,000 production budget\;
  accommodation for two months divided between Helsinki and Turku\, one mon
 th in each\; travel costs for one return ticket from a Nordic-Baltic count
 ry\; access to Titanik's residency studio space and a working desk at M-Cu
 lt's office during each stay\; mentoring and curatorial support from both 
 organisations' staff\; and networking into the Finnish media art and conte
 mporary art scenes. In return the artist develops in-depth or focused rese
 arch and presents their practice and research at two public events\, one i
 n each city. WHO CAN APPLY: individual artists only\, explicitly NOT colle
 ctives this round\; artists from or based in Finland\, Sweden\, Norway\, D
 enmark\, Iceland\, Aland\, the Faroe Islands\, Greenland\, Estonia\, Latvi
 a or Lithuania\; working in sound\, media and/or digital arts\, or the exp
 anded field of vernacular technologies\, all defined broadly by the organi
 sers. Applicants must be available to travel to Finland for the full two-m
 onth period across February and March 2027. The organisers welcome applica
 nts at all career stages and from all backgrounds. One submission per arti
 st: if two are sent\, only the later one is reviewed. HOW TO APPLY: submit
  via the form linked from the open call page with a brief letter of motiva
 tion including a research plan for the residency\, how it connects with th
 e programme's themes and what you would focus on (max 1-2 pages)\, your CV
 \, and a link to your portfolio. Applications in English only. DEADLINE: 3
 0 August 2026 at 23:59 UTC+3. Online interviews with shortlisted artists t
 ake place before 19 September 2026\, and all applicants are notified by em
 ail by the end of September 2026. JURY: Jussi Koitela\, Director of M-Cult
 \, Helsinki\, and Farbod Fakharzadeh\, Director of Arte ry and Titanik\, T
 urku. ACCOMMODATION AND ACCESSIBILITY: in Helsinki\, the Vallila Residency
  hosted by M-Cult is a 30 sqm apartment in a small wooden house with one r
 oom\, kitchen and bathroom with shower\; it is NOT fully accessible\, sitt
 ing on the first floor up stairs with no elevator (details from info@m-cul
 t.org). In Turku\, the Titanik A.i.R. apartment is 27 sqm on the top floor
  of a building with an elevator\, but the space including the bathroom is 
 not fully accessible (details from info@titanik.fi). A partner\, friend or
  child may join\, but their expenses are not covered. THE PARTNERS: M-Cult
 \, founded in 2000\, develops and presents art and media culture with a fo
 cus on the social and political dimensions of media and technology\, worki
 ng through art commissions\, residencies and learning programmes. Titanik\
 , established in Turku in 1988 by the artist-run organization Arte Ry\, ha
 s since 2006 run Titanik A.i.R.\, the first artist residency in Finland wi
 th a focus on sound art and sonic practices. CONTACT: Jussi Koitela (jussi
 .koitela@m-cult.org) or Farbod Fakharzadeh (director@arte.fi).\n\nOrganisa
 tion: Art and Media Culture Agency M-Cult (Helsinki) and Arte artists' ass
 ociation / Titanik gallery (Turku)\nLocation: Finland\; one month in Helsi
 nki and one month in Turku. Open to artists from or based in Nordic and Ba
 ltic countries.\nAward: EUR 3\,500 artist fee plus EUR 2\,000 production b
 udget\, two months' accommodation split between Helsinki and Turku\, and o
 ne return travel ticket from a Nordic-Baltic country. No application fee s
 tated.\nDuration: Two months\, February to March 2027 (one month in each c
 ity)\n\nMore: https://www.titanik.fi/residency-open-call-residing-non-line
 ar-technologies-and-sonic-worldings/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.titanik.fi/residency-open-call-residing-non-linear-technolo
 gies-and-sonic-worldings/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium
 =referral
LOCATION:Finland\; one month in Helsinki and one month in Turku. Open to ar
 tists from or based in Nordic and Baltic countries.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:foodculture-days-kitchen-central-location-2027@artificialnouveau.github
 .io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260831
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260901
SUMMARY:Deadline: The Kitchen / Central Location Open Call (foodculture day
 s Biennale\, Vevey 2027)
DESCRIPTION:foodculture days is opening up The Kitchen / Central Location\,
  the living heart of its biennale in Vevey\, to an outside collective for 
 the festival's 6th edition. The Kitchen is at once an open-air kitchen\, a
  gathering space and an artistic installation\, sited by the lake on the E
 splanade de la Paix along a busy promenade\, hosting multidisciplinary pro
 jects\, concerts\, themed meals\, public discussions\, citizens' assemblie
 s and moments of collective cooking. The call asks for new ways of inhabit
 ing it. WHO THEY WANT: a transdisciplinary collective of scientists\, arti
 sts\, designers\, craftspeople\, cooks\, activists and architects\, either
  newly formed or already active\; collaboration across generations\, cultu
 res and levels of expertise is encouraged. WHAT IS OFFERED: an open-air ci
 tizen experimentation laboratory in Vevey's public space\, framed around r
 ethinking ways of living and the relationship to time and to creation\, an
 d thinking together about the conditions under which multidisciplinary pra
 ctices can flourish. THE BRIEF: kitchen and hospitality\, lunch and dinner
  service\, vegetarian meals with a vegan option. Meals should be affordabl
 e\, seasonal where fresh produce is involved\, and conceived in the spirit
  of a communal canteen: simple\, generous\, nourishing and full of flavour
 . Expected covers are roughly 100 guests Wednesday to Thursday and roughly
  150 Friday to Sunday. WHAT THE FESTIVAL PROVIDES: curatorial support to d
 evelop the proposal\, with particular attention to the themed meals\; intr
 oductions to local producers\, growers and artisans including farm visits 
 and foraging sites\; production support and volunteers throughout\; and st
 andard professional kitchen equipment and cooking facilities. BUDGET: CHF 
 15\,000 all-inclusive (VAT included) covering travel\, visas\, equipment r
 ental\, any additional kitchen equipment\, per diems\, materials and artis
 t fees\; food costs and accommodation in Vevey are covered separately. THE
  SPACE: the pavilion\, called Cuisine\, is a modular metal structure assem
 bled from repurposed agricultural greenhouse components on a 3.1 metre bid
 irectional grid\, with pillars and arches forming ridge vaults\, a textile
  covering naturally dyed yellow with reseda\, and a terracotta brick heart
 h for wood-fired cooking laid directly on the floor. It comes with dining 
 tables\, low tables\, a reception table\, a shelf\, a bar\, pendant lights
 \, 30 cushions\, removable curtains\, flags\, blackboards and signage pane
 ls\, and can expand\, contract or be reconfigured. TIMELINE: Phase 1 deadl
 ine 31 August 2026 at midnight CET\; three shortlisted proposals selected 
 in late September\, each invited to an online meeting and paid a CHF 250 r
 esearch fee for Phase 2\; final project selected and announced in early Oc
 tober 2026\; collaborative development with the foodculture days architect
 ural team October to November\; production December to February\; build an
 d installation in Vevey 1 to 16 June 2027\, with the collective present th
 roughout those two weeks\; 6th edition of the biennale 16 to 20 June 2027.
  PHASE 1 QUESTIONS: tell us about your collective (origins\, intention\, w
 hat makes you special)\; member biographies with collective or individual 
 portfolios\, website\, Instagram\, city of residence and practices\; what 
 the concept consists of in terms of food and cuisine\, relationships\, and
  scenography and spatial research\; what you want to put into practice in 
 the central pavilion\, your vision and the kind of experience you want to 
 create\; any special requirements\; and references\, including a quote rep
 resenting the collective\, two reference texts\, three images and optional
 ly video. An Open Call Information Kit\, a recording of the online informa
 tion session and a Q&A are published on the open call site and are worth r
 eading before applying.\n\nOrganisation: foodculture days\nLocation: Vevey
 \, Switzerland. The Kitchen is built on the Esplanade de la Paix by the la
 keside. The selected collective must be present in Vevey for the two-week 
 build and installation\, 1 to 16 June 2027\, and through the biennale 16 t
 o 20 June 2027.\nAward: CHF 15\,000 all-inclusive project budget (VAT incl
 uded)\, covering travel\, visas\, equipment and additional kitchen equipme
 nt rental\, per diems\, materials and artist fees. Food costs and accommod
 ation in Vevey are covered separately by foodculture days. Three shortlist
 ed collectives each receive a CHF 250 research fee to develop their propos
 al in Phase 2. One collective is selected. No application fee.\nDuration: 
 October 2026 to June 2027: collaborative development October-November\, pr
 oduction December-February\, on-site build 1-16 June 2027\, biennale 16-20
  June 2027\n\nMore: https://opencall.foodculturedays.com/en?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://opencall.foodculturedays.com/en?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Vevey\, Switzerland. The Kitchen is built on the Esplanade de la P
 aix by the lakeside. The selected collective must be present in Vevey for 
 the two-week build and installation\, 1 to 16 June 2027\, and through the 
 biennale 16 to 20 June 2027.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:teatri-riflessi-2027-short-performance-competition@artificialnouveau.gi
 thub.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261016
SUMMARY:Deadline: Teatri Riflessi 2027: Short Performance Competition (12th
  edition)
DESCRIPTION:An open call for at least 10 short performances of maximum 15 m
 inutes for the 12th edition of Teatri Riflessi in Zafferana Etnea\, Sicily
 . THE FORMAT: the competition champions the short performance in its own r
 ight\, not as a reduction of a longer work nor as a sketch for a full-even
 ing adaptation\; its strength is the artistic immediacy and urgency it car
 ries. The framing connects ancient Greek theatre\, conceived as an outdoor
  competition for a large audience\, to the more provocative tendencies of 
 happenings and performance art that lean on the beholder's desire to parti
 cipate. STRUCTURE: semi-finalists perform on the evenings of Thursday 15 a
 nd Friday 16 July 2027\; the Programmers' Panel and the Scholars' & Critic
 s' Panel determine the finalists\, who perform again in the final on Sunda
 y 18 July. The panels bring together around 30 Italian and international a
 rtistic directors\, curators\, festival and theatre programmers\, journali
 sts\, critics and performing arts scholars\, many from the Teatri Riflessi
  Network and Anticorpi XL Network\; the full list is published in June 202
 7. Past partner organisations include Antistatic Festival (Sofia)\, ATER F
 ondazione\, BIG Festival\, Cantieri Danza\, Circuito CLAPS\, COORPI\, Danc
 e ICONS (Washington DC)\, Danza Urbana\, Derida Dance Centre\, EN-KNAP and
  Spanski Borci (Ljubljana)\, Fabbrica Europa\, Festival Ammutinamenti\, Cl
 uny Danse (France)\, Danza Canarias dentro y fuera (Tenerife)\, FIND Festi
 val\, Fondazione Armunia and Festival Inequilibrio\, Fondazione Claudia Lo
 mbardi per il teatro (Lugano)\, Fondazione Sipario Toscana\, Fondazione To
 scana Spettacolo\, Galway Dance (Ireland)\, Interplay Festival (Turin)\, L
 'Arboreto Teatro Dimora\, La Piccionaia\, Movimento Danza\, New Dance For 
 Asia International Festival (Daegu)\, Puglia Culture\, Toplocentrala (Sofi
 a) and Umbria Danza Festival. MONEY: each selected performance receives a 
 gross fee of EUR 500 to EUR 1\,100 depending on cast size\, plus a possibl
 e travel contribution of up to EUR 250. Awards are Best Performance EUR 1\
 ,200 (from the combined weighted scores of both panels\, the Jury of the F
 inal\, the Youth Jury and the Citizens' Jury)\, Best Dramaturgy EUR 500 an
 d the Scholars' and Critics' Award EUR 500 (both from the Scholars' & Crit
 ics' Panel)\, Best Direction EUR 500 and Best Performer EUR 500 (both from
  the Programmers' Panel)\, the 'Valentina Nicosia' Fund of EUR 500 (joint 
 decision of both panels)\, the 'Sandra Bressan' research fund of EUR 1\,80
 0 (awarded by the Citizens' Jury to reinvite a company to Sicily to work w
 ith the community)\, and the Youth Jury Award of EUR 300 to a semi-finalis
 t\, alongside the Audience Special Mention\, the Companies' Choice Award a
 nd the Technical Crew Award. Fees\, reimbursements and prizes are paid aft
 er the festival\, provided all regulations and deadlines are met. FEES TO 
 APPLY: none. Only selected companies pay a EUR 50 deposit on selection\, f
 ully refunded after the festival. RULES: performances should aim for 15 mi
 nutes\, with total stage occupancy including set-up and dismantling capped
  at 20 minutes. Multiple entries are allowed but need a separate form each
 . No major changes are permitted after selection\; minor adjustments\, esp
 ecially cast substitutions\, must be communicated in advance and authorise
 d by IterCulture APS. Works in languages other than Italian are welcome an
 d are presented with Italian and English surtitles prepared by IterCulture
  APS. APPLICATION: a digital form linked in Article 5 of the open call reg
 ulations\, with Annex A for dramaturgy (the complete script where one exis
 ts\, or for dance\, physical theatre and non-text work a short document on
  the dramaturgical research and choreographic structure) and a full video 
 recording of the complete work\; excerpts and teasers are not accepted\, a
 nd for rehearsed readings\, directorial notes on costumes\, lighting and s
 et design are mandatory. COMMITMENT: rehearsal attendance is compulsory\, 
 with the day assigned by the Competition Manager after selection\; compani
 es must arrive in Zafferana Etnea by their rehearsal day (rehearsals run 1
 3 and 14 July 2027) and stay until the festival closes at 23:30 on Sunday 
 18 July. Rehearsals and public events run mainly in afternoons and evening
 s\; the only compulsory morning commitment is the panel feedback session o
 n Sunday 18 July. Online information sessions are held on Google Meet on T
 uesday 22 September 2026\, with the English session at 19:30 CEST. Deadlin
 e 15 October 2026 at 5pm CET.\n\nOrganisation: IterCulture APS\nLocation: 
 Zafferana Etnea\, Sicily\, Italy. Open to Italian and international compan
 ies and artists. Semi-finals 15 and 16 July 2027\, final 18 July 2027\; re
 hearsals 13 and 14 July.\nAward: Gross performance fee of EUR 500 to EUR 1
 \,100 (VAT included) per selected short performance\, scaled by the number
  of performers on stage\, plus a possible travel contribution of up to EUR
  250 subject to available funding\, place of origin\, cast size and absenc
 e of external touring grants. At least 10 performances are selected. Compe
 tition prizes: Best Performance EUR 1\,200\; Best Dramaturgy\, Best Direct
 ion\, Best Performer and the Scholars' and Critics' Award EUR 500 each\; '
 Valentina Nicosia' Fund EUR 500\; 'Sandra Bressan' research fund EUR 1\,80
 0\; Youth Jury Award EUR 300\; plus non-cash awards (Audience Special Ment
 ion\, Companies' Choice\, Technical Crew). Panel members and Teatri Rifles
 si Network partners may also award special prizes in the form of artist re
 sidencies and touring opportunities. Application is free\; selected compan
 ies pay a EUR 50 deposit that is fully refunded after the festival.\nDurat
 ion: Festival participation 13 to 18 July 2027\, with mandatory rehearsals
  and presence until 23:30 on 18 July\n\nMore: https://www.iterculture.eu/e
 n/teatri-riflessi/tr2027/tr12/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_m
 edium=referral
URL:https://www.iterculture.eu/en/teatri-riflessi/tr2027/tr12/?utm_source=a
 rtificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Zafferana Etnea\, Sicily\, Italy. Open to Italian and internationa
 l companies and artists. Semi-finals 15 and 16 July 2027\, final 18 July 2
 027\; rehearsals 13 and 14 July.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mpi-empirical-aesthetics-inhabit-16-17-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: INHABIT #16 and #17: Artist-in-Residence 2027 (Max Planck
  Institute for Empirical Aesthetics)
DESCRIPTION:INHABIT is the artist-in-residence programme of the Max Planck 
 Institute for Empirical Aesthetics in Frankfurt am Main\, which invites ar
 tists from various disciplines to collaborate with its scientists and rese
 archers\, treating artistic thinking and knowledge as reflective practices
  in their own right. The 2027 call is addressed to artists from the perfor
 ming arts and music\, who spend four months creating new work\, or develop
 ing an existing project\, inside a scientific research environment and in 
 dialogue with the institute's researchers. Two slots are open for 2027: IN
 HABIT #16 from April to July 2027 and INHABIT #17 from September to Decemb
 er 2027. Work developed during the residency is presented in cooperation w
 ith local arts institutions as an exhibition\, performance\, concert or ot
 her format\, complemented by discursive formats. WHO THEY ARE LOOKING FOR:
  artists from the performing arts and music interested in interdisciplinar
 y collaboration between artistic and scientific fields\; artists open to d
 eveloping and sharing a project as an exhibition\, performance\, concert o
 r another format\; and artists active in contemporary culture who respond 
 to the institute with innovative and challenging ideas. WHAT IS OFFERED: a
 n artist's fee of EUR 8\,000\, an accommodation fee of EUR 2\,000\, a proj
 ect-dependent production budget\, travel costs to and in Frankfurt\, reali
 sation of the final project\, collaborations with scientists\, access to t
 he library\, sound studio and scientific facilities\, and curatorial suppo
 rt during the residency. APPLY through the institute's e-recruiting portal
  by 1 September 2026\, 23:59 CET\; the jury decision follows in November 2
 026. No fee.\n\nOrganisation: Max Planck Institute for Empirical Aesthetic
 s\nLocation: Frankfurt am Main\, Germany\nAward: Artist's fee of EUR 8\,00
 0 plus an accommodation fee of EUR 2\,000\, a production budget depending 
 on the project\, and travel costs to and within Frankfurt. Also included: 
 realisation of the final project\, collaborations with scientists\, access
  to the institute's library\, sound studio and scientific facilities\, and
  curatorial support throughout the residency. No application fee.\nDuratio
 n: Four months. Two slots: INHABIT #16 runs April to July 2027\, INHABIT #
 17 runs September to December 2027\n\nMore: https://www.aesthetics.mpg.de/
 en/research/inhabit-artist-in-residence.html?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.aesthetics.mpg.de/en/research/inhabit-artist-in-residence.h
 tml?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Frankfurt am Main\, Germany
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tartu-city-of-literature-residency-autumn-2026@artificialnouveau.github
 .io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Tartu UNESCO City of Literature Residency for Writers and
  Translators\, Autumn 2026
DESCRIPTION:The Estonian Literary Society\, which coordinates Tartu UNESCO 
 City of Literature\, runs an international residency programme for writers
  and translators that has hosted authors from Slovenia\, Ireland\, Hungary
 \, the USA\, the UK\, Ukraine and Canada since 2017. This is the open call
  for the autumn 2026 slot: one resident stays two months in the Karl Risti
 kivi residency apartment in Tartu\, working on their own writing or transl
 ation while connecting with the local literary scene. WHAT THE RESIDENCY O
 FFERS: a EUR 600 monthly stipend\, travel reimbursement up to EUR 350\, fr
 ee accommodation\, a local support coordinator to help arrange cultural en
 gagements\, and opportunities to perform and present at literary events. T
 he autumn period covers the interdisciplinary literary festival Crazy Tart
 u on 12 to 14 November\, and the resident is offered a slot to perform the
 re alongside writers\, poets\, musicians and artists from Estonia and abro
 ad. ELIGIBILITY: open to writers\, poets and translators of Estonian liter
 ature of any nationality\; applicants need an upper-intermediate level of 
 spoken English\, at least one published book\, screenplay\, theatre script
  or translation from Estonian into another language\, a demonstrable inter
 est in Estonian culture and literature\, a willingness to take part in loc
 al literary activities\, and a commitment to working on their own literary
  project during the stay. HOW TO APPLY: complete the online application fo
 rm linked from the residency page and upload a fragment of up to five page
 s of a published text (in Estonian or English) or of a published translati
 on. SELECTION: made by a committee representing the Estonian Literary Soci
 ety\, the Estonian Writers Union\, the Estonian Literary Museum and the Ta
 rtu Literature House Foundation. Results are announced before 15 September
  2026. The programme's stated aims are to enhance international exchange\,
  diversify the local literary scene\, introduce new foreign authors and th
 eir work to Estonian readers\, and build lasting connections beyond the re
 sidency period. Questions: Marja Unt\, eks@kirjandus.ee. Deadline 1 Septem
 ber 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Estonian Literary Society (Eesti Kirjanduse Sel
 ts)\, Focal Point for Tartu UNESCO City of Literature\nLocation: Tartu\, E
 stonia. Open to writers\, poets and translators of Estonian literature wor
 ldwide.\nAward: Monthly stipend of EUR 600 for the two-month stay (EUR 1\,
 200 in total)\, plus reimbursement of travel costs up to EUR 350. Free acc
 ommodation is provided in the Karl Ristikivi residency apartment\, which h
 as a bedroom\, living room\, kitchen\, bathroom and exhibition room. One r
 esident is selected. No application fee.\nDuration: Two months\, 15 Octobe
 r to 15 December 2026\, with some flexibility on exact dates\n\nMore: http
 s://tartu.kirjandus.ee/residency-autumn-2026?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://tartu.kirjandus.ee/residency-autumn-2026?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Tartu\, Estonia. Open to writers\, poets and translators of Estoni
 an literature worldwide.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:archipel-butor-livre-de-dialogue-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260830
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260831
SUMMARY:Deadline: Archipel Butor Livre de dialogue Creation Residency 2027
DESCRIPTION:Archipel Butor runs its creation residency out of the former ho
 me of the writer Michel Butor in Lucinges\, Haute-Savoie\, and this call i
 s for a livre de dialogue\, a dialogue book made jointly by a writer and a
  visual artist. The residency exists to give a pair concentrated time to d
 evelop a book together and to raise the profile of artist book culture and
  of collaboration at the centre of artistic process. WHO APPLIES: a pair m
 ade up of an author with a project for a dialogue book and a visual artist
  collaborating on it. The two do not need to have worked together before\,
  but both must be present during the shared periods. WHAT IS PROVIDED: EUR
  2\,000 gross per month per artist\, up to two return trips per person wit
 hin France and Europe\, and accommodation in the writer's house. STRUCTURE
 : two months in total\, taken as eight weeks which may be split across the
  year from January 2027\, with 70 percent of the time given to creation an
 d 30 percent to mediation and public engagement activities. A videoconfere
 nce is held with the selected laureates beforehand to arrange on-site sche
 duling and the mediation sessions. HOW TO APPLY: follow the official call 
 document downloadable from the residency page\, submitting a single PDF to
  accueil@archipel-butor.fr containing a joint letter\, biographies of both
  practitioners\, the artistic proposal\, technical specifications and the 
 proposed mediation activities. NOTE: the call and application file are in 
 French. Deadline 30 August 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Archipel Butor\nLocation
 : Lucinges (74380)\, Haute-Savoie\, France\, in the house of the writer Mi
 chel Butor.\nAward: Creation grant of EUR 2\,000 gross per month per artis
 t\, so roughly EUR 4\,000 each across the two months and EUR 8\,000 for th
 e pair. Up to two return journeys per person are covered within France and
  Europe. Accommodation is provided in Michel Butor's writer's house. No ap
 plication fee.\nDuration: Two months in total\, taken as eight weeks that 
 may be split\, starting from January 2027. Time is split 70 percent creati
 on and 30 percent mediation activities.\n\nMore: https://www.archipel-buto
 r.fr/residence-creation/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=
 referral
URL:https://www.archipel-butor.fr/residence-creation/?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Lucinges (74380)\, Haute-Savoie\, France\, in the house of the wri
 ter Michel Butor.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:les-antipodes-numeric-2026-the-word@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260908
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260909
SUMMARY:Deadline: Numeric 2026: The Word (Les antipodes Research and Creati
 on Residency)
DESCRIPTION:Two research and creation residency grants in Agullana\, Catalo
 nia\, for artists\, thinkers and scientists of any branch (formal\, natura
 l\, social\, applied) working at the intersection of art\, culture\, scien
 ce and thought. THIS YEAR'S THEME\, The Word\, is squarely about large lan
 guage models. The framework moves from the word as creative principle acro
 ss traditions (the Judeo-Christian creating God\, the Quran as uncreated w
 ord\, the Sanskrit Om and the Vedas\, mantras that summon rather than desc
 ribe) to science relocating that intuition in the cell (Sagan's four-lette
 r alphabet of DNA as a material text\, Margulis countering that the langua
 ge of life is chemistry\, Witzany holding that all cell interactions are s
 ign-mediated)\, and then to LLMs\, which for the first time detach the wor
 d from the flesh and generate text through a probabilistic architecture tr
 ained on human language. The call asks what LLMs reveal about authorship\,
  originality and meaning when a system generates text that moves\, persuad
 es or deceives without experience or intention\, and whether we can still 
 say the models operate exclusively on human experience once they ingest th
 eir own output. It explicitly wants work that blurs comprehension and simu
 lation\, authorship and recombination\, and it names antecedents worth kno
 wing before applying: Ramon Llull's Ars Magna\, Joan Brossa's Sextina cibe
 rnetica\, Oulipo constraint writing\, oracles and divination\, oral-formul
 aic transmission\, translation as probabilistic approximation\, exquisite 
 corpses\, Burroughs's cut-ups\, automatic writing\, musical improvisation 
 and scientific simulation. Les antipodes asks for engagement 'beyond the i
 nstrumental use of the tools' and away from utopian and dystopian framings
 . WHAT YOU GET: spacious\, luminous\, independent work spaces plus a share
 d terrace in the centre of the village\, spaces for meeting\, dialogue and
  public presentation\, introductions to local\, academic\, artistic and pr
 ofessional contacts on request\, and support organising any activities tha
 t arise. The residency ends with an informal presentation\, and results ma
 y feed into the publications or public programme of Les antipodes. IMPORTA
 NTLY\, this is not an acquisition prize and involves no transfer of rights
 : authorship and intellectual property stay with the creators\, and select
 ion implies no acquisition of the work. Credits on resulting work must ack
 nowledge Numeric 2026 and its collaborators. WHO CAN APPLY: open to everyo
 ne of legal age\, any discipline or origin\, individually or as a collecti
 ve\, with the stipend shared among collective members. Applications must b
 e in Catalan or English whatever the working language of the project\, sub
 mitted through the online form with an optional PDF of up to 5 pages and 1
 0 MB. One application per person or collective. EVALUATION\, in order of w
 eight: singularity and innovation\; relevance to this year's LLM framework
 \; and interaction and transfer of value\, meaning relations with the soci
 al and geographical environment of Agullana and the Emporda and a plan for
  presenting the outcome in editorial\, on-site\, performative\, sound\, au
 diovisual or other form. The call may be declared void if no proposal reac
 hes the required level. PRACTICAL: residents must hold their own health co
 ver (EHIC for EU citizens\, or valid travel or health insurance for Spain 
 otherwise) and are responsible for their own equipment. Supported by the G
 eneralitat de Catalunya\, Agullana and Figueres town councils\, and Accion
  Cultural Espanola through the PICE national residencies programme. Terms 
 are published in Arabic\, Catalan\, English\, Spanish\, French and Chinese
 .\n\nOrganisation: Les antipodes\, with Bolit Centre d'Art Contemporani Gi
 rona and Museu de l'Emporda Figueres\nLocation: Agullana\, Alt Emporda\, C
 atalonia\, Spain. A village of 900 people\, 20 km from Figueres and the Vi
 lafant high-speed rail station\, 40 km from Perpignan\, 60 km from Girona\
 , 160 km from Barcelona.\nAward: Two grants. Each provides a stipend of EU
 R 1\,000 as taxable base (taxes and withholdings apply)\, round-trip trave
 l within the European Union\, and accommodation and meals for the four wee
 ks in Agullana. Travel and meals cover the resident only\, though the shar
 ed apartment can host immediate family by arrangement. Numeric also provid
 es the resources specified in the application and agreed during preparatio
 n. No application fee. Note that if a selected candidate lacks the profess
 ional registration needed to receive the stipend and payment has to be arr
 anged through Les antipodes\, the resulting costs are deducted from the st
 ipend.\nDuration: Four weeks\, 2 to 30 November 2026\, with both residenci
 es running simultaneously. Preceded by one month of preparation and follow
 ed by a two-month closing period. Applications 23 July to 8 September 2026
 \; decision announced 22 September 2026.\n\nMore: https://lesantipodes.com
 /numeric/2026_bases_en.html?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medi
 um=referral
URL:https://lesantipodes.com/numeric/2026_bases_en.html?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Agullana\, Alt Emporda\, Catalonia\, Spain. A village of 900 peopl
 e\, 20 km from Figueres and the Vilafant high-speed rail station\, 40 km f
 rom Perpignan\, 60 km from Girona\, 160 km from Barcelona.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:le-garage-moderne-oasis-residencies-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Le Garage Moderne: OASIS International Artist Residencies
  2026 (Bordeaux)
DESCRIPTION:Second year of Le Garage Moderne's residency cycle within the E
 uropean OASIS project\, offering five grants to international artists for 
 two-week stays in Bordeaux. THE SITE IS THE POINT. Le Garage Moderne is a 
 working non-profit car and bicycle workshop with a neighbourhood canteen a
 nd a versatile venue for performing arts\, concerts and community gatherin
 gs\, all at once a productive space\, a public space and a community-drive
 n common. Having just moved back into its 19th-century building after a lo
 ng renovation\, the team describes machines and workbenches back in place 
 and a brand-new playground\, and invites residents to take over the space 
 and explore its physical and social possibilities. They ask for SITE-SPECI
 FIC PROPOSALS that play with the verticality\, the scale of the space\, th
 e community and what they call the hive-like vibe of the venue\, where eve
 ryone runs around\, shouts\, gets their hands dirty and learns in the proc
 ess. DISCIPLINES: any\, explicitly including design\, visual art\, perform
 ing arts\, film\, small-scale architecture\, emergency architecture\, craf
 t-making\, street furniture\, sound\, and interdisciplinary or community-b
 ased practices. Proposals combining artistic creation with the spatial and
  the social are especially encouraged\, and the organisers say plainly tha
 t they want to be surprised. WHAT IS EXPECTED: openness to exchange and co
 llaboration with the 11 permanent residents and with 3 local artists recru
 ited through a separate OASIS call\; participation in 2 days of masterclas
 s open to members and community\, where you describe and share your practi
 ce\, technique and working context with fellow OASIS residents\, local art
 ists\, members and staff\; and a public outcome\, which need not be a larg
 e event but must be something the public can experience. RIGHTS: work prod
 uced during the residency remains the artist's property\, but documentatio
 n of it is made by Le Garage Moderne and will be publicised by them for th
 ree years after the residency. Note this is a different OASIS partner call
  from the OASis In the Park (Naples) and Disappearing Landscape (High Tatr
 as) rounds under the same European project.\n\nOrganisation: Le Garage Mod
 erne (European OASIS project)\nLocation: Bacalan district\, Bordeaux\, Fra
 nce. Le Garage Moderne is a non-profit car garage and bicycle workshop\, a
  canteen serving sponsored meals\, and a cultural venue housing 11 permane
 nt artists\, makers and craftswomen\, recently returned to its 19th-centur
 y building after a two-and-a-half-year renovation.\nAward: Five grants. Ea
 ch artist receives a fee of EUR 1\,300 gross (taxes may apply depending on
  legal status)\, up to EUR 600 for production expenses such as raw materia
 ls\, technical services or special tools\, a lump-sum travel grant scaled 
 to distance with top-ups for green travel options\, a per diem of EUR 45 p
 er day\, and accommodation in a self-catering hotel. Access to the shared 
 tools and spaces of Le Garage Moderne is included\, subject to the associa
 tion's regulations. No application fee.\nDuration: Two weeks on site. Five
  overlapping two-week slots\, and applicants may choose one or more: 9 to 
 22 November\, 16 to 29 November\, 23 November to 6 December\, 30 November 
 to 13 December\, and 7 to 20 December 2026. Deadline 1 September 2026\; pr
 e-selection interviews 15 September\; final selection announced 1 October 
 2026.\n\nMore: https://legaragemoderne.org/oasis2026?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://legaragemoderne.org/oasis2026?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Bacalan district\, Bordeaux\, France. Le Garage Moderne is a non-p
 rofit car garage and bicycle workshop\, a canteen serving sponsored meals\
 , and a cultural venue housing 11 permanent artists\, makers and craftswom
 en\, recently returned to its 19th-century building after a two-and-a-half
 -year renovation.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:unidee-cittadellarte-visiting-research-curator-2027-28@artificialnouvea
 u.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260913
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260914
SUMMARY:Deadline: UNIDEE Residency Programs: Visiting Research Curator 2027
 -28
DESCRIPTION:Cittadellarte is recruiting a Visiting Research Curator to shap
 e the research arc of the UNIDEE Residency Modules for 2027-2028\, the rol
 e most recently held by Nina Fiocco and Gaia Martino. Founded by Michelang
 elo Pistoletto in 1999\, the residency has hosted thousands of artists and
  cultural professionals from 52 countries. WHAT THEY WANT: rather than a f
 ixed theme set in advance\, they want a curator who brings their own line 
 of inquiry and develops it collectively through the modules. Suggested the
 matic areas are the evolving landscape of socially engaged art practices\,
  research-driven and process-oriented practice\, and the conditions of cul
 tural work and cultural workers\, aligned with UNIDEE's focus on artistic 
 research in response to ecological\, geopolitical and technological challe
 nges. They also flag a specific interest in how contemporary art practices
  are archived\, drawing on the UNIDEE archive\, which documents over two d
 ecades of socially engaged art initiatives. THIS IS A JOB\, NOT A GRANT: t
 he duties list is long and operational. It covers proposing the overarchin
 g curatorial theme\, designing and delivering a minimum of 8 weekly reside
 ntial modules per year\, writing the curatorial statement and resident ope
 n call\, recruiting mentors and guests\, selecting residents\, hosting and
  facilitating every module in person\, communications and website texts\, 
 a dissemination strategy\, and conceiving and editing publications. There 
 is also teaching-adjacent work with the Unidee Academy of Contemporary Art
 s\, including public lectures and studio visits. Budget the time before ap
 plying. PROFILE: experience curating art in the public sphere and socially
  engaged art\, specialised knowledge of international contemporary art\, e
 xperience designing experimental and collaborative educational activities\
 , and experience with artistic research and dissemination standards. Excel
 lent English required\; Italian welcome but not essential. APPLYING: onlin
 e form with a project proposal of maximum 5000 characters stating your vis
 ion for the modules programme and a development strategy including possibl
 e mentors and guests\, plus a CV\, a portfolio of maximum three relevant p
 rojects\, and TWO LETTERS OF RECOMMENDATION\, so line up your referees ear
 ly. A jury of the UNIDEE Advisory Board\, the Director of Cittadellarte an
 d invited experts decides. They do not give feedback on unsuccessful propo
 sals.\n\nOrganisation: Fondazione Pistoletto Cittadellarte and UNIDEE Resi
 dency Programs\nLocation: Cittadellarte\, Biella\, Italy. Requires in-pers
 on presence at Cittadellarte for a minimum of one month plus the full leng
 th of each module.\nAward: Compensation and contractual terms commensurate
  with the candidate's level of professional experience\, starting from a g
 ross amount of EUR 22\,000 for the appointment\, excluding travel and hosp
 itality\, which are covered separately. No application fee.\nDuration: Tem
 porary appointment from November 2026 to December 2028\, covering the 2027
 -2028 research arc and a minimum of 8 residency modules per year. Deadline
  13 September 2026 at 23:59 CEST\; shortlisted candidates interviewed onli
 ne by mid-October 2026\, with the selected candidate announced a few days 
 later.\n\nMore: https://unidee.cittadellarte.it/activity.html?id=269&utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://unidee.cittadellarte.it/activity.html?id=269&utm_source=artific
 ialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Cittadellarte\, Biella\, Italy. Requires in-person presence at Cit
 tadellarte for a minimum of one month plus the full length of each module.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:eofa-artistic-research-residency-geneva-2027@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Deadline: Embassy of Foreign Artists: Artistic Research Residency i
 n International Organisation Archives (Geneva\, 2027)
DESCRIPTION:The Embassy of Foreign Artists\, in partnership with the Centre
  for Digital Humanities and Multilateralism at the Geneva Graduate Institu
 te\, invites artists worldwide to a three-month artistic research residenc
 y in Geneva during 2027. The programme centres on archival research in the
  archives of Geneva-based international intergovernmental and non-governme
 ntal organisations (UN\, Red Cross and others): uncovering untold stories\
 , examining international decision-making\, reflecting on multilateral suc
 cesses and failures\, and imagining new possibilities for international co
 operation. Selected artists receive a CHF 1\,400 monthly residency grant\,
  accommodation in a private room with shared common areas\, artistic guida
 nce from EOFA\, connections with archive personnel\, and access to partici
 pating archives as primary research resource\; travel and production costs
  are the artist's own. ELIGIBILITY: professional artistic practice with a 
 demonstrable body of work (creations\, publications and/or performances)\,
  over 28 years old\, fluent in French or English\, not enrolled in basic a
 rt training\; individuals\, duos or groups may apply (same stipend). APPLY
  via the online form plus a single PDF (cover letter\, project description
 \, portfolio\, CV) emailed to application@eofa.ch. No application fee. Dea
 dline: 15 September 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Embassy of Foreign Artists / Ce
 ntre for Digital Humanities and Multilateralism\, Geneva Graduate Institut
 e\nLocation: Geneva\, Switzerland\nAward: CHF 1\,400 monthly residency gra
 nt plus accommodation in a private room\; travel and artistic production c
 osts are not covered\nDuration: 3 months\, during 2027\n\nMore: https://ww
 w.eofa.ch/en/open-call/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=r
 eferral
URL:https://www.eofa.ch/en/open-call/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Geneva\, Switzerland
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:welcome-to-my-homepage-oulu-edition-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261016
SUMMARY:Deadline: Welcome to my Homepage: Online Net Art Residency\, Oulu E
 dition
DESCRIPTION:Welcome to my Homepage is an international online residency hos
 ted by The Museum of Human Achievement in Austin\, Texas\, offering artist
 s a low-stakes opportunity to experiment\, explore the web as a site for c
 reative production\, and reach new audiences with net art (artwork created
  on and experienced exclusively through the internet). Founded in 2014\, i
 t has hosted over 150 artists. THIS ROUND (Oulu Edition) is open only to a
 pplicants in the Oulu\, Finland area\, as a collaboration between the UNES
 CO Cities of Media Arts Oulu and Austin\, and especially seeks proposals t
 hat consider digital culture from a northern perspective\, bring an Arctic
  point of view\, or take inspiration from the edges rather than the center
 . Selected residents (3 per cycle) receive a EUR 500 stipend\, the mmm.pag
 e drag-and-drop web builder (no coding needed\; hosting on your own domain
  is also fine)\, virtual studio visits\, mentor conversations and promotio
 n. Projects are shown online at welcometomyhomepage.net and in person at p
 op-up exhibitions alongside 3 Austin artists at the Frozen People Festival
  in Oulu and at MoHA in Austin. WHO IT IS FOR: all types of creative folks
 \, no coding necessary and no need to be a net or digital artist (past res
 idents include performers\, poets\, puppeteers\, filmmakers\, healthcare w
 orkers and musicians)\; the programme especially welcomes people who have 
 not had an opportunity like this before\, would benefit from a flexible on
 line residency\, or want time to experiment. Collectives can apply via a p
 rimary contact. NOT ELIGIBLE: applicants outside the Oulu area (this round
  only)\, under-18s\, undergrad or grad students enrolled in an art\, desig
 n or media programme during the residency\, and full-time university facul
 ty in such programmes. Jurors look for thoughtful\, interesting\, fun or c
 hallenging proposals achievable within the 3-week online residency\; propo
 sals for existing creative projects\, promotional pages (portfolio or band
  sites) or projects relying heavily on visitor submissions are less succes
 sful\, and the work should be experienceable fully from the browser. APPLI
 CATION: statement of interest or residency proposal (max 300 words)\, arti
 st statement (max 200 words)\, bio (max 200 words)\, and work samples (up 
 to 4 links and/or a PDF of up to 10 images)\; brief and honest is preferre
 d over fancy and academic. Selection is by a jury of Oulu Urban Culture st
 aff\, an Oulu artist\, MoHA staff and a past resident\, led by Residency D
 irector Rachel Stuckey. Applicant info session online on 1 October 2026\, 
 5pm EEST. Notification by late October 2026. Deadline 15 October 2026\, 23
 :59 EEST. The next call open to applicants from anywhere is expected in ea
 rly 2027.\n\nOrganisation: The Museum of Human Achievement (MoHA)\, Austin
 \, TX\, with Oulu UNESCO City of Media Arts\, Oulu Urban Culture and Froze
 n People\nLocation: Fully online residency. This round is restricted to ap
 plicants based in Oulu\, Finland and surrounding areas (a UNESCO Cities of
  Media Arts collaboration between Oulu and Austin). Pop-up showcases at th
 e Frozen People Festival in Oulu and at MoHA in Austin.\nAward: EUR 500 st
 ipend\, plus a user-friendly web builder (mmm.page)\, virtual studio visit
 s and mentor conversations\, promotion\, a year-round showcase at welcomet
 omyhomepage.net and a kiosk at the Austin Public Library's Innovate Lab\, 
 and in-person pop-up exhibitions at the Frozen People Festival in Oulu and
  at MoHA in Austin (Austin installation handled by the organisers\; no res
 ident travel funds to Austin). Free to apply.\nDuration: Online residency 
 8 to 31 January 2027 (about 3 weeks)\; Frozen People show in mid/late Febr
 uary 2027\; MoHA show and virtual artist talk in spring 2027\n\nMore: http
 s://welcometomyhomepage.net/apply?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&ut
 m_medium=referral
URL:https://welcometomyhomepage.net/apply?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Fully online residency. This round is restricted to applicants bas
 ed in Oulu\, Finland and surrounding areas (a UNESCO Cities of Media Arts 
 collaboration between Oulu and Austin). Pop-up showcases at the Frozen Peo
 ple Festival in Oulu and at MoHA in Austin.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stroom-den-haag-pro-art-projects-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261025
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261026
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stroom Den Haag: PRO Art Projects
DESCRIPTION:Stroom Den Haag's PRO Art Projects scheme contributes to the co
 sts of realising a contemporary art project. WHO CAN APPLY: artists\, cura
 tors\, critics\, publicists\, partnerships and organisations. Applicants d
 o not have to live in The Hague: Hague artists apply via their Stroom data
 base registration (Mijn Stroom)\, while applicants from outside the city a
 pply with a CV\, provided the project takes place in The Hague or otherwis
 e benefits art and artists in The Hague. ASSESSMENT: quality and distincti
 veness of the project\, whether it represents a step in a new direction\, 
 an experiment or a departure\, its contribution to The Hague's art climate
 \, and proportionality between budget and scope. APPLICATION: via the Stro
 om portal with a plan of max 2\,500 words (artistic rationale\, target aud
 ience\, evaluation)\, an itemised budget using Stroom's model\, and image 
 documentation. NOT ELIGIBLE: applications connected to formal (art) educat
 ion programmes or from current students (Bachelor\, Master\, postdoc\, PhD
 ). DEADLINE: the last 2026 round closes 25 October 2026 (rounds recur roug
 hly every six weeks through the year). The grant is valid for up to two ye
 ars after the decision\, with 80 percent paid upfront.\n\nOrganisation: St
 room Den Haag\nLocation: The Hague\, Netherlands. Open to applicants from 
 outside The Hague (apply with a CV) as long as the project takes place in 
 The Hague or otherwise benefits art and artists in The Hague\; Hague artis
 ts must be registered in the Stroom database (Mijn Stroom).\nAward: Maximu
 m EUR 10\,000 per project\, up to EUR 20\,000 per applicant per calendar y
 ear. Requests above EUR 5\,000 require at least 30 percent co-financing of
  the total budget from third parties. Artist fees\, production and communi
 cation costs are eligible\; Stroom endorses the kunstenaarshonorarium.nl f
 ee guideline. No application fee.\nDuration: Project-based\; the grant rem
 ains valid for up to two years after the decision meeting\, with 80 percen
 t paid upfront and 20 percent on the final report\n\nMore: https://www.str
 oom.nl/en/stroom-for-artists/financial-support/pro-art-projects?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stroom.nl/en/stroom-for-artists/financial-support/pro-art-p
 rojects?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:The Hague\, Netherlands. Open to applicants from outside The Hague
  (apply with a CV) as long as the project takes place in The Hague or othe
 rwise benefits art and artists in The Hague\; Hague artists must be regist
 ered in the Stroom database (Mijn Stroom).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:anima-brussels-festival-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261002
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261003
SUMMARY:Deadline: Anima 2027: Brussels International Animation Film Festiva
 l Submissions
DESCRIPTION:Anima\, the Brussels International Animation Film Festival\, is
  open for submissions for its 46th edition (19 to 28 February 2027). CATEG
 ORIES: feature films\, feature films for children\, international professi
 onal short films\, international student films\, international short films
  for children\, national (Belgian) short films\, and short films in virtua
 l reality. Films must be completed after June 2025. Submissions are free v
 ia the festival's online form until 2 October 2026. Winners in the main co
 mpetitions receive cash prizes and an Anima trophy\; the prize list for 20
 27 is published in late January. Anima is an Academy Award and BAFTA quali
 fying festival\, and a small\, approachable festival for animated and anim
 ation-adjacent experimental work. Notification to filmmakers on 4 December
  2026.\n\nOrganisation: Anima\, Brussels International Animation Film Fest
 ival\nLocation: Brussels\, Belgium. Open internationally\; separate nation
 al (Belgian) short film competition.\nAward: Free to submit until 2 Octobe
 r 2026. Winners in the main competition categories receive cash prizes plu
 s an Anima trophy (the 2027 prize list is published in late January 2027).
  The festival is an Academy Award and BAFTA qualifying festival for eligib
 le films.\nDuration: Festival 19 to 28 February 2027\; notification 4 Dece
 mber 2026\n\nMore: https://animafestival.be/en/festival/film-submission?ut
 m_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://animafestival.be/en/festival/film-submission?utm_source=artific
 ialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Brussels\, Belgium. Open internationally\; separate national (Belg
 ian) short film competition.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kaboom-animation-festival-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261005
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261006
SUMMARY:Deadline: Kaboom Animation Festival 2027: Call for Entries
DESCRIPTION:Kaboom Animation Festival\, the Netherlands' largest animation 
 festival\, is accepting films\, games and VR projects for its 2027 edition
  in Amsterdam and Utrecht. Kaboom takes a famously broad view of what coun
 ts as animation: experimental and hybrid work screens alongside traditiona
 l animation\, and combinations of animation and live-action are eligible a
 s long as the larger part of the work is animated\, which makes it a plaus
 ible home for AI-generated and expanded-media video work. In recent editio
 ns animated shorts could run up to 30 minutes excluding credits with up to
  3 submissions per filmmaker\; check the current regulations on the submis
 sion portal. Submissions are free of charge via the FilmChief portal. DEAD
 LINE: 5 October 2026\, 23:59 CET.\n\nOrganisation: Kaboom Animation Festiv
 al\nLocation: Amsterdam and Utrecht\, Netherlands. Open internationally.\n
 Award: No entry fee for submitting to Kaboom's competitions. Competition a
 wards are given across categories (amounts not published in the call)\; th
 e festival is known for an open\, experimental definition of animation.\nD
 uration: Festival in March 2027 across Amsterdam and Utrecht\n\nMore: http
 s://www.kaboomfestival.nl/news/call-for-entries-2027-is-now-open/?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.kaboomfestival.nl/news/call-for-entries-2027-is-now-open/?u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Amsterdam and Utrecht\, Netherlands. Open internationally.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:go-short-nijmegen-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261215
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261216
SUMMARY:Deadline: Go Short 2027: International Short Film Festival Nijmegen
  Submissions
DESCRIPTION:Go Short\, the international short film festival in Nijmegen\, 
 is open for entries for its 19th edition (6 to 11 April 2027). A small\, a
 pproachable Dutch festival that programmes fiction\, documentary\, animati
 on and experimental shorts. COMPETITIONS: the European Competition (fictio
 n\, documentary\, animation\, experimental)\, the Dutch Competition\, and 
 the New Arrivals Competition for European film school projects\, plus a Mu
 sic Video Competition and a separate strand for video games\, VR/XR\, perf
 ormances and installations\, which makes it a natural target for expanded-
 media and installation-based video work. DEADLINES AND FEES: early bird 15
  September 2026 (EUR 12.50 per film\; EUR 8 per installation/VR/game proje
 ct)\, regular 15 November (EUR 15 / EUR 10)\, late 15 December 2026 (EUR 2
 0 / EUR 12)\; music videos EUR 7.50 flat. Awards include Best European Sho
 rt\, Best Dutch Short\, the New Arrivals Award and an Audience Award. Read
  the festival regulations for length and completion date requirements befo
 re submitting.\n\nOrganisation: Go Short\, International Short Film Festiv
 al Nijmegen\nLocation: Nijmegen\, Netherlands. European Competition open t
 o films made in Europe\; dedicated Dutch Competition\; New Arrivals Compet
 ition for European film school projects.\nAward: Small submission fees per
  tier: EUR 12.50 (early bird\, 15 September 2026)\, EUR 15 (regular\, 15 N
 ovember) or EUR 20 (late\, 15 December) for films\; EUR 8/10/12 for video 
 games\, VR/XR\, performances and installations\; EUR 7.50 flat for music v
 ideos. Awards include the Go Short Award for Best European Short\, Best Du
 tch Short\, the New Arrivals Award and an Audience Award (amounts not publ
 ished in the call).\nDuration: Festival 6 to 11 April 2027\n\nMore: https:
 //www.goshort.nl/en/news-overview/call-for-entry-go-short-2027?utm_source=
 artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.goshort.nl/en/news-overview/call-for-entry-go-short-2027?ut
 m_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Nijmegen\, Netherlands. European Competition open to films made in
  Europe\; dedicated Dutch Competition\; New Arrivals Competition for Europ
 ean film school projects.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cultural-horizons-residencies-subgrants-2027@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: Cultural Horizons Residencies: Subgrants for EU Organisat
 ions Hosting Ukrainian Artists
DESCRIPTION:Cultural Horizons strengthens the cultural sector in Ukraine by
  promoting joint EU-Ukrainian cultural initiatives and expanding access fo
 r Ukrainians affected by the war to European cultural and artistic network
 s. The Residencies strand provides subgrants for EU-based institutions to 
 implement (a) residency placements and/or (b) education projects organised
  on the basis of residencies\, for and with Ukrainian artistic and cultura
 l professionals in 2027. WHO CAN APPLY: artistic and cultural organisation
 s and initiatives registered within the EU\; consortia designate one lead 
 organisation to submit and manage funding. Applicants must demonstrate the
  ability to host Ukrainian artistic and cultural professionals in 2027 and
  complete projects between January and August 2027\, confirm the absence o
 f ties with the Russian Federation (no working partnerships with Russia or
  Russian organisations\, no visits to Russian-occupied territories after 2
 014)\, commit to refraining from glorification of Russian imperialism\, co
 mply with the EU sanctions regime\, and demonstrate a commitment to divers
 ity\, equity and inclusion. NGOs and public sector institutions working wi
 th displaced and vulnerable groups are prioritised. WHO IT SUPPORTS: Ukrai
 nian artists and cultural practitioners (independent and employed professi
 onals\, early-career specialists\, debut artists\, cultural managers\, res
 earchers\, analysts\, conservators)\, vulnerable groups from Ukraine inclu
 ding internally displaced persons\, young artists and communities in front
 line and conflict-affected areas\, and Ukrainian cultural organisations wi
 th a focus on small communities\, local initiatives\, independent cultural
  spaces and NGOs. TIMELINE: applications 29 June to 30 September 2026\; ev
 aluation October to November 2026\; implementation 1 January to 30 July 20
 27. The programme runs 2026-2027 and also builds a Europe-wide network of 
 cultural expert mentors. Queries: culturalhorizons[at]culturalvistas.eu.\n
 \nOrganisation: Ukrainian Cultural Foundation and Cultural Vistas\, funded
  by the Creative Europe Programme of the European Union\nLocation: Europea
 n Union. Open to artistic and cultural organisations and initiatives regis
 tered within the EU\; residency and education projects host Ukrainian arti
 stic and cultural professionals during 2027.\nAward: Subgrants of EUR 5\,0
 00 to 20\,000 each\; a minimum of 20 subgrants will be awarded. No applica
 tion fee.\nDuration: Projects run 1 January to 30 July 2027\, minimum 3 an
 d maximum 8 months\; final reports due within one month of completion and 
 no later than 15 August 2027\n\nMore: https://culturalvistas.eu/our-progra
 ms/professional-study-tours/cultural-horizons?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral#residencies
URL:https://culturalvistas.eu/our-programs/professional-study-tours/cultura
 l-horizons?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral#resid
 encies
LOCATION:European Union. Open to artistic and cultural organisations and in
 itiatives registered within the EU\; residency and education projects host
  Ukrainian artistic and cultural professionals during 2027.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:braunschweig-projects-hbk-fellowships-2027-28@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261004
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261005
SUMMARY:Deadline: Braunschweig Projects 2027/28: Artistic Fellowships at HB
 K Braunschweig (Fine Arts and Sound Art)
DESCRIPTION:With Braunschweig Projects\, HBK Braunschweig (one of Germany's
  largest art academies\, with fine arts\, art education\, performing arts\
 , design\, visual communication\, art history and media studies) offers 7 
 artistic fellowships on behalf of the State of Lower Saxony for 2027/28: 5
  in fine arts and 2 in sound art. The programme promotes young artists and
  internationalisation\, and is aimed at artists who want to work on a proj
 ect in the immediate vicinity of HBK\; proposals should make a significant
  contribution to the further development of forms of artistic practice. Ea
 ch fellow is assigned a self-chosen mentor from the fine arts professors\,
  all professors of the fine arts department are available for artistic dis
 course\, and fellows can present their project's progress within the unive
 rsity. Fellows are expected to participate in the Welcome Weeks (19 to 30 
 April 2027) and a joint final presentation in January/February 2028\, and 
 must reside at HBK for at least 8 months during the summer and winter seme
 ster lecture periods. FUNDING: EUR 1\,600 per month for 12 months from 1 A
 pril 2027\, a rent-free one-person studio apartment (EUR 250 per month con
 tribution to incidental costs)\, and an allowance for project and travel c
 osts\; a short final report (about 1 page) is due at the end. ELIGIBILITY:
  a successfully completed art degree\, with the most recent studies comple
 ted after 31 March 2016 and before 1 April 2023\; proof of extensive artis
 tic practice and exhibition participation\; no regular third-party benefit
 s (salary\, work scholarships or state subsidy) during the funding period.
  APPLICATION: in German or English by email to application-bsprojects[at]h
 bk-bs.de\, addressed to President Prof. Dr. Ana Dimke\, with the completed
  and signed application form\, an artistic profile (one file\, max 15MB: n
 ame\, website and social media\, artist statement max 350 words\, project 
 description max 350 words\, portfolio of 10 to 15 works\, short CV\, links
  to 3 password-free video/audio files) and the diploma of the most recent 
 degree (PDF\, max 1MB). DEADLINE: 4 October 2026. A separate Braunschweig 
 Projects curatorial fellowship for 2027/28 runs in parallel.\n\nOrganisati
 on: Braunschweig University of Art (HBK Braunschweig)\, on behalf of the S
 tate of Lower Saxony\nLocation: Braunschweig\, Germany. Open international
 ly (application in German or English)\; fellows must reside at HBK for at 
 least 8 months during the lecture periods.\nAward: Stipend of EUR 1\,600 p
 er month for 12 months\, plus a rent-free one-person studio apartment in B
 raunschweig (fellows pay EUR 250 per month towards incidental living costs
 ) and an allowance for project and travel costs. 7 fellowships: 5 in fine 
 arts and 2 in sound art. No application fee.\nDuration: 12 months from 1 A
 pril 2027 (accommodation from 15 April 2027)\; Welcome Weeks 19 to 30 Apri
 l 2027\; joint final presentation January/February 2028\n\nMore: https://w
 ww.hbk-bs.de/hochschule/stipendienprogramme/braunschweig-projects-deutsch/
 ausschreibung-bewerbung-1?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium
 =referral
URL:https://www.hbk-bs.de/hochschule/stipendienprogramme/braunschweig-proje
 cts-deutsch/ausschreibung-bewerbung-1?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Braunschweig\, Germany. Open internationally (application in Germa
 n or English)\; fellows must reside at HBK for at least 8 months during th
 e lecture periods.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ses12naus-two-phase-residency-2026-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: Fundacion Ses12naus: Two-Phase Residency for Visual Artis
 ts and Curators\, Ibiza (2026-2027)
DESCRIPTION:Ses12naus\, a non-profit founded in 2016 to strengthen the cult
 ural and artistic fabric of Ibiza and develop the island as an internation
 al reference for contemporary artistic creation\, is launching a two-phase
  residency for visual artists and curators at any career stage. Four proje
 cts are selected for the 2026-2027 edition: two by artists or curators bas
 ed in the Balearic Islands\, one from the rest of Spain and one from anoth
 er European country. STRUCTURE: Phase 1 (21 November to 13 December 2026) 
 is dedicated to research and exploration of the territory and an in-depth 
 understanding of the local context\, with a required public activity linke
 d to the process\; between phases the Foundation's team actively follows u
 p on the conceptualisation and formalisation of the proposal\; in Phase 2 
 (17 May to 7 June 2027) residents return to produce and present: artists p
 roduce their works\, curators continue their research\, and both present r
 esults. The format supports developing a new project or giving continuity 
 to an ongoing one\, in dialogue with Ibiza and its communities. FUNDING: E
 UR 1\,800 honorarium plus EUR 300 public-activity fee per resident\; trave
 l up to EUR 330 (Spain) or EUR 770 (Europe) booked by the Foundation (no t
 ravel between phases is financed)\; production up to EUR 3\,000 for artist
 s plus EUR 500 installation and EUR 200 public-activity costs (curators: E
 UR 500 plus EUR 200). RESOURCES: private bedroom and bathroom with shared 
 kitchen and living room\, a workspace at La Carpinteria sized to the proje
 ct with projectors\, speakers\, machinery and tools (specific materials no
 t in the inventory come from the production budget)\, production assistanc
 e\, a shared car for the duration (valid driving licence required) and air
 port transfers. APPLICATION: online form\, deadline 30 September 2026\, 23
 :59 CET.\n\nOrganisation: Fundacion Ses12naus\nLocation: Ibiza\, Balearic 
 Islands\, Spain (at La Carpinteria creation centre\, Can Bufi). Open to vi
 sual artists and curators residing in the Balearic Islands\, Spain and Eur
 ope: of four selected projects\, two go to the Balearic Islands\, one to t
 he rest of Spain and one to another European country. No age limit.\nAward
 : Honorarium of EUR 1\,800 per resident (EUR 900 per phase) plus EUR 300 f
 or the public activity (all subject to taxes and withholdings). Travel up 
 to EUR 330 for participants from Spain or EUR 770 from other European coun
 tries (booked by the Foundation). Production: artists up to EUR 3\,000 for
  production and public presentation (including transport of the work)\, pl
 us up to EUR 500 installation costs and EUR 200 for public activities\; cu
 rators up to EUR 500 for the final presentation and EUR 200 for the public
  activity. Also included: private bedroom with private bathroom\, shared k
 itchen and living room\, workspace at La Carpinteria with technical resour
 ces\, production assistance\, a shared car (driving licence required) and 
 airport transfers. Free to apply.\nDuration: Two 3-week phases: 21 Novembe
 r to 13 December 2026 (research and territory exploration\, with a public 
 activity) and 17 May to 7 June 2027 (production and presentation)\, with a
 ctive follow-up between phases\n\nMore: https://ses12naus.org/en/applicati
 on-form-open-call-2026-2027/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
URL:https://ses12naus.org/en/application-form-open-call-2026-2027/?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Ibiza\, Balearic Islands\, Spain (at La Carpinteria creation centr
 e\, Can Bufi). Open to visual artists and curators residing in the Baleari
 c Islands\, Spain and Europe: of four selected projects\, two go to the Ba
 learic Islands\, one to the rest of Spain and one to another European coun
 try. No age limit.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:perform-europe-open-call-2026-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261022
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261023
SUMMARY:Deadline: Perform Europe: Open Call 2026-2028 (cross-border touring
 )
DESCRIPTION:Perform Europe is the EU support scheme for cross-border tourin
 g and distribution of performing arts works across Creative Europe countri
 es. WHAT IT FUNDS: touring of completed performing arts works (all perform
 ing arts disciplines except live music and opera)\; it does NOT cover prod
 uction costs for new creations. Each proposal must present at least one ar
 tistic work in at least three different Creative Europe countries. GRANTS:
  EUR 15\,000\, EUR 25\,000 or EUR 55\,000 depending on project size\, with
  top-ups of up to EUR 5\,000 per proposal for sustainability and accessibi
 lity measures (maximum EUR 60\,000 total). WHO IS ELIGIBLE: partnerships o
 f at least three partners from at least three Creative Europe countries (t
 he 27 EU member states plus 14 non-EU participating countries)\; organizat
 ions and professionals in the performing arts sector. DEADLINE: 22 October
  2026\, 23:59 CEST. TO APPLY: via the Perform Europe platform linked from 
 the call page. Free to apply.\n\nOrganisation: Perform Europe (co-funded b
 y Creative Europe\, European Union)\nLocation: Creative Europe countries (
 27 EU member states plus 14 non-EU participating countries). Each partners
 hip needs at least three partners from at least three Creative Europe coun
 tries.\nAward: Three grant tiers: EUR 15\,000 (small)\, EUR 25\,000 (mediu
 m) or EUR 55\,000 (large) per proposal\, plus top-ups of up to EUR 5\,000 
 for sustainability and accessibility needs\; absolute maximum EUR 60\,000 
 per proposal including top-ups. No application fee.\nDuration: Touring pro
 jects within the 2026-2028 Perform Europe cycle\n\nMore: https://culture.e
 c.europa.eu/funding/calls/open-call-of-perform-europe-2026-2028?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://culture.ec.europa.eu/funding/calls/open-call-of-perform-europe-
 2026-2028?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Creative Europe countries (27 EU member states plus 14 non-EU part
 icipating countries). Each partnership needs at least three partners from 
 at least three Creative Europe countries.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:emaf-2027-call-for-entries@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261215
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261216
SUMMARY:Deadline: EMAF 2027: Call for Entries\, Film / Installation / Expan
 ded
DESCRIPTION:The European Media Art Festival (EMAF) in Osnabrueck invites su
 bmissions for its 2027 edition in three sections: Film (experimental films
  of all lengths and any theme)\, Installation (installative\, interactive\
 , spatial or sculptural media art works) and Expanded (performances\, live
  events or workshops). WHAT YOU GET: all films selected for the Internatio
 nal Selection are equal winners of the EMAF Award with EUR 400 prize money
  each\; films in the Features section (over 60 minutes) receive a EUR 250 
 screening fee\; curated programmes pay EUR 80-250 depending on length\; in
 stallations and expanded projects receive a EUR 500 fee with production co
 sts paid by the festival. Selected artists are invited to the festival wit
 h free accreditation\, three hotel nights (potentially longer if setting u
 p is required) and a contribution to travel costs. RULES: maximum 2 works 
 per artist\; only works completed in 2026 or 2027 are eligible\; no premie
 re status required\; works entered at previous editions will not be recons
 idered. Films up to 60 minutes are viewed for the International Selection\
 , films over 60 minutes for Features. Installation entries should relate t
 o the 2027 festival theme of the archive (as an instrument of knowledge pr
 oduction\, a site of critical intervention and a space for alternative vis
 ions of the future)\; Installation and Expanded entries must include a com
 prehensive description\, tech rider\, cost calculation and visual material
 s. Non-English-language works must have English subtitles for the selectio
 n screening. Submit digitally via the EMAF registration portal (no DVDs or
  physical media). Selection decisions are emailed from mid-March 2027. DEA
 DLINE: the call closes as soon as 2\,200 entries have been received\, or a
 t the latest on 15 December 2026\, so submit early. No entry fee.\n\nOrgan
 isation: European Media Art Festival (EMAF)\nLocation: Osnabrueck\, German
 y. Open worldwide\; selected artists are invited to the festival with free
  accreditation\, three hotel nights and a contribution to travel costs.\nA
 ward: All films in the International Selection are equal winners of the EM
 AF Award and receive EUR 400 each. Screening fees: EUR 250 for Features\, 
 EUR 80-250 for curated programmes depending on length\, EUR 500 for instal
 lations and expanded projects\; production costs for installations and exp
 anded projects are paid by the festival. Selected artists get free accredi
 tation\, three hotel nights (longer if setup requires) and a travel cost c
 ontribution. No entry fee.\nDuration: Festival in Osnabrueck\, spring 2027
 \; screening prints must arrive by 1 April 2027\n\nMore: https://emaf.film
 chief.com/entry-forms?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=ref
 erral
URL:https://emaf.filmchief.com/entry-forms?utm_source=artificialnouveaugran
 tdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Osnabrueck\, Germany. Open worldwide\; selected artists are invite
 d to the festival with free accreditation\, three hotel nights and a contr
 ibution to travel costs.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mq-air-2027-vienna-whw@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Deadline: MQ Artist-in-Residence Programme 2027\, Vienna
DESCRIPTION:The MQ Artist-in-Residence (MQ AiR) programme offers artists th
 e opportunity to step away from everyday production pressure and focus on 
 a specific artistic interest or research project\, living and working in o
 ne of the MQ studios in the MuseumsQuartier in the heart of Vienna. This 2
 027 call is run with tranzit and the WHW Akademija (supported by Erste Fou
 ndation and the Igor Zabel Association). SUPPORT: EUR 1\,300 monthly stipe
 nd and a EUR 300 travel grant (EUR 500 for participants from outside the E
 U)\, plus the live-work MQ studio. TO APPLY: send your application with th
 e subject line 'MQ AiR 2027' to office@tranzit.org\; the full call details
  and application form are at akademija.whw.hr. DEADLINE: 15 September 2026
  at midnight.\n\nOrganisation: MuseumsQuartier Wien (MQ AiR)\, with tranzi
 t and WHW Akademija\nLocation: MuseumsQuartier\, Vienna\, Austria. Live-wo
 rk residency in one of the MQ studios\; non-EU participants are eligible (
 higher travel grant).\nAward: EUR 1\,300 monthly stipend plus a EUR 300 tr
 avel grant (EUR 500 for non-EU participants). Live-work studio at the Muse
 umsQuartier included.\nDuration: Residency during 2027 in an MQ studio in 
 Vienna\n\nMore: https://www.akademija.whw.hr?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.akademija.whw.hr?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_
 medium=referral
LOCATION:MuseumsQuartier\, Vienna\, Austria. Live-work residency in one of 
 the MQ studios\; non-EU participants are eligible (higher travel grant).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:dcc-ballyfermot-library-visual-arts-commission-2027@artificialnouveau.g
 ithub.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261016
SUMMARY:Deadline: Dublin City Council: Visual Arts Exhibition Commission fo
 r Ballyfermot Library (curated by IMMA)
DESCRIPTION:Dublin City Council's Creative Hubs programme\, delivered by Th
 e Ark and curated by IMMA (Irish Museum of Modern Art)\, invites submissio
 ns for its 5th Visual Arts Exhibition Commission: an exhibition created fo
 r children\, schools and families\, located in Ballyfermot Library for app
 roximately 10 weeks from April to June 2027. Proposals should respond to a
  general theme of nature and the natural world\, in line with IMMA's ongoi
 ng programme on climate\, culture and collective action (Earth Rising). Th
 e commissioned exhibition must give children under 12 a quality visual art
 s experience\, engage with the library setting and the Ballyfermot context
 \, and include opportunities for children to experience the artist's proce
 ss (a studio visit or field trip plus an audio or video interview by child
 ren before the exhibition opens)\; the artist also contributes to an educa
 tion and learning programme led by IMMA. Previous commissions in the serie
 s went to Aideen Barry (2015)\, Barbara Knezevic (2019)\, Jane Locke (2022
 ) and Lucy McKenna (2024). WHAT YOU GET: EUR 10\,000 for research and deli
 very of the commissioned works\, technical installation support from IMMA\
 , mentorship from the Arts Office if requested\, and an associated educati
 on programme run by IMMA across the exhibition's run. APPLICATION: a short
  proposal\, a brief history of your work and the principles of your practi
 ce\, and a broad outline of your idea for an accessible and engaging visua
 l arts exhibition for children\; submitted via the Dublin City Arts Office
  Submittable page. Assessment: quality visual arts experience for children
  30 percent\, engagement with the library context 20 percent\, cognisance 
 of the target age group and input on the engagement programme 30 percent\,
  feasibility and R&D structure 20 percent. A maximum of five proposals are
  shortlisted\; shortlisted artists meet representatives of the Arts Office
 \, Dublin City Libraries\, The Ark and IMMA on 29 October 2026\, with the 
 award notified in the week of 2 November 2026. DEADLINE: 15 October 2026\,
  12 noon.\n\nOrganisation: Dublin City Council Creative Hubs programme\, d
 elivered by The Ark\, curated by IMMA (Irish Museum of Modern Art)\nLocati
 on: Ballyfermot Library\, Dublin\, Ireland. The call does not state a resi
 dency or nationality restriction\; shortlisted artists meet the panel on 2
 9 October 2026 and the commission involves in-person engagement with child
 ren in Dublin (a studio visit or field trip and an interview by children).
 \nAward: EUR 10\,000 commission award for research and delivery of commiss
 ioned works for the exhibition. Technical support for installation is prov
 ided by IMMA\, and the artist is supported by Arts Office and Library staf
 f during the research phase. No application fee.\nDuration: Exhibition run
 s approximately 10 weeks\, April to June 2027\, in the exhibition room of 
 Ballyfermot Library\n\nMore: https://dublincityartsoffice.submittable.com/
 submit?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://dublincityartsoffice.submittable.com/submit?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Ballyfermot Library\, Dublin\, Ireland. The call does not state a 
 residency or nationality restriction\; shortlisted artists meet the panel 
 on 29 October 2026 and the commission involves in-person engagement with c
 hildren in Dublin (a studio visit or field trip and an interview by childr
 en).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
