UID:oberhausen-73-call-for-films-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270118
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270119
SUMMARY:Deadline: Internationale Kurzfilmtage Oberhausen: Call for Films\, 
 73rd Festival (2027)
DESCRIPTION:The 73rd International Short Film Festival Oberhausen (27 April
  to 2 May 2027)\, one of the oldest and most influential short film festiv
 als\, opens its call for films across five competitions: International (ma
 x 35 minutes\, produced outside Germany\, German festival premiere require
 d)\, German (max 45 minutes\, produced in Germany\, no premiere requiremen
 t)\, NRW (max 45 minutes\, produced or co-produced in North Rhine-Westphal
 ia)\, International Children's and Youth Film\, and the MuVi Award for mus
 ic videos produced in Germany (max 15 minutes). ELIGIBILITY: works produce
 d after 1 January 2026\; screening formats 35mm\, 16mm\, Super 8 and DCP (
 MuVi: DCP). PRIZES: from the EUR 8\,000 Grand Prize of the City of Oberhau
 sen and EUR 4\,000 Principal Prize through German\, NRW\, children's/youth
 \, FIPRESCI\, Ecumenical and audience prizes\, awarded to the directors\, 
 plus European Film Awards and ECFA nominations. FEES: the first five submi
 ssions per submitter are free of charge\; from the sixth\, a EUR 20 handli
 ng fee per film applies. HOW TO SUBMIT: online entry form with preview lin
 k via kurzfilmtage.filmchief.com\; selection results announced mid-March 2
 027. DEADLINE: 18 January 2027 for all competitions (17:00 UTC per the lis
 ting)\, except the MuVi Award: 22 February 2027. No extensions.\n\nOrganis
 ation: Internationale Kurzfilmtage Oberhausen (International Short Film Fe
 stival Oberhausen)\nLocation: Oberhausen\, Germany. International Competit
 ion open to productions from outside Germany (plus co-productions)\; separ
 ate German\, NRW\, Children's and Youth\, and MuVi competitions.\nAward: I
 nternational Competition: Grand Prize of the City of Oberhausen EUR 8\,000
 \, Principal Prize EUR 4\,000\, Promotional Prize EUR 1\,500\, plus a Euro
 pean Film Awards short film nomination. German Competition: EUR 5\,000 mai
 n prize\, EUR 1\,500 promotional\, EUR 2\,500 3sat Emerging Talent Prize (
 with purchase offer)\, EUR 1\,000 ZONTA Prize for a female filmmaker. NRW 
 Competition: EUR 1\,000 and EUR 500 prizes\, plus NRW Ministry prizes of E
 UR 5\,000 and EUR 3\,000\, FIPRESCI Prize\, EUR 2\,000 Ecumenical Jury Pri
 ze\, EUR 750 WDR Westart Audience Jury Prize. Children's and Youth: severa
 l EUR 1\,000-1\,500 prizes and an ECFA Short Film Award nomination. Prizes
  go to the directors. SUBMISSION FEE: first five submissions per submitter
  are free\; EUR 20 handling fee per film from the sixth.\nDuration: Festiv
 al runs 27 April to 2 May 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.kurzfilmtage.de/en/fe
 stival/submission/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referr
 al
URL:https://www.kurzfilmtage.de/en/festival/submission/?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Oberhausen\, Germany. International Competition open to production
 s from outside Germany (plus co-productions)\; separate German\, NRW\, Chi
 ldren's and Youth\, and MuVi competitions.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:art-explora-cite-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261030
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261031
SUMMARY:Deadline: Art Explora x Cité internationale des arts Residency\, 7
 th Call (Paris)
DESCRIPTION:The 7th call of the Art Explora residency programme at the Cit
 é internationale des arts opened 21 September 2026. The programme support
 s projects exploring the crossovers of art with science\, technology and e
 cology\, which makes it one of the stronger art-science fits in Europe. Re
 sidents receive a furnished live-work studio of around 50 m2 in Paris\, EU
 R 1\,000 per month living stipend\, up to EUR 3\,000 production budget\, r
 ound-trip travel and mentoring\, with residencies of 3 or 6 months for sol
 o artists and 3 months for duos of an artist with a researcher\, curator o
 r writer. Open to visual\, performing and digital artists of all nationali
 ties and ages with at least 5 years of professional experience and an inte
 rnational exhibition record. Programme details at artexplora.org. TO APPLY
 : submit via the Art Explora application platform. DEADLINE: 30 October 20
 26\, 11:59 PM Paris time.\n\nOrganisation: Art Explora Foundation and Cit
 é internationale des arts\nLocation: Paris\, France. Open worldwide to ar
 tists with at least 5 years of professional practice.\nAward: EUR 1\,000 p
 er month living stipend plus up to EUR 3\,000 production grant\, a furnish
 ed live-work studio of around 50 m2 at the Cité internationale des arts\,
  round-trip travel to Paris and curatorial mentoring. No application fee.\
 nDuration: 3- or 6-month residencies during 2027\; 3 months for duos (arti
 st plus researcher\, curator or writer).\n\nMore: https://artexplora.plate
 formecandidature.com/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=ref
 erral
URL:https://artexplora.plateformecandidature.com/?utm_source=artificialnouv
 eaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Paris\, France. Open worldwide to artists with at least 5 years of
  professional practice.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:after-the-palace-resonance-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261030
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261031
SUMMARY:Deadline: AFTER THE PALACE: Resonance 2026 Video Mapping Contest (K
 rakow)
DESCRIPTION:AFTER THE PALACE: Resonance 2026 is an international video mapp
 ing competition and outdoor showcase that asks digital media artists to cr
 eatively reinterpret the dissonant heritage of socialist-era architecture 
 in the context of the history\, cultural identity and memory of Krakow's N
 owa Huta. Artists\, animators\, motion designers\, creative teams and stud
 ios worldwide are invited to create original site-specific projections for
  the courtyard facade of Building Z of the New Administrative Centre\, for
 merly part of the Lenin Steelworks. Organised by the University of the Nat
 ional Education Commission in Krakow as part of the international artistic
  and research project unLoc. TECHNICAL: 2D/3D video mapping with sound\, 1
  to 8 minutes\, MP4 (H.264/AAC) in 4K at 25 fps\, minimum 40 Mbps\, audio 
 48 kHz/16-bit\, built on the dedicated building mapping matrix from the do
 cument package. Generative AI tools are permitted provided their use is fu
 lly disclosed in the application form and the applicant holds rights to th
 e source materials. TIMELINE: submission deadline 30 October 2026\, 23:59 
 CET\; results by 10 November\; outdoor showcase and award ceremony 23 Nove
 mber 2026 in the courtyard at 1 Ujastek St\, Krakow. TO APPLY: submit the 
 online application form with a download link to the work\; the full regula
 tions and mapping matrix are at unloc.art. Contact unloc@uken.krakow.pl.\n
 \nOrganisation: University of the National Education Commission in Krakow 
 (unLoc project)\nLocation: Krakow-Nowa Huta\, Poland. Fully digital submis
 sion from anywhere\; showcase 23 November 2026 on the facade of Building Z
 \, New Administrative Centre (former Lenin Steelworks).\nAward: Cash prize
 s: PLN 10\,000 (~EUR 2\,340) first place\, PLN 6\,000 second\, PLN 3\,000 
 third\; the jury may award additional honorary distinctions or redistribut
 e the pool. Free to enter\, submission is exclusively digital.\n\nMore: ht
 tp://unloc.art/en/news/after-the-palace-en/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:http://unloc.art/en/news/after-the-palace-en/?utm_source=artificialnouv
 eaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Krakow-Nowa Huta\, Poland. Fully digital submission from anywhere\
 ; showcase 23 November 2026 on the facade of Building Z\, New Administrati
 ve Centre (former Lenin Steelworks).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ernest-albert-invitational-artistic-development-residency-2027@artifici
 alnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261028
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261029
SUMMARY:Deadline: Ernest Albert Invitational 2027: Artistic Development Res
 idency at Cas-co x Kunsthal Mechelen
DESCRIPTION:Cas-co and Kunsthal Mechelen invite four Belgium-based early-ca
 reer visual artists to the Ernest Albert Invitational 2027\, a four-month 
 Artistic Development Residency at Cas-co in Leuven within the Off the Grid
  programme\, running in parallel with a Reflective Residency for a researc
 her who accompanies the group. Residents receive a studio\, curatorial gui
 dance and peer exchange\, and develop new work towards a group exhibition 
 at Kunsthal Mechelen\, 4 June to 29 August 2027\, curated by Jessica Meule
 man (Kunsthal Mechelen)\, Zuzanna Rachowska and Arthur Cordier (Cas-co). T
 HEME: the edition departs from landscape understood as a field of relation
 s shaped by memory\, ecology\, migration and lived experience\, and welcom
 es practices that move between inner and outer worlds across installation\
 , performance\, moving image\, sound and other experimental forms. SUPPORT
 : EUR 1\,100 artist fee per month\, EUR 120 transportation allowance per m
 onth\, and a one-time production budget of EUR 1\,200 (EUR 6\,080 total in
 cluding VAT)\, plus additional artist and production fees from Kunsthal Me
 chelen for the exhibition. ELIGIBILITY: Belgium-based visual artists at an
  early stage of their career with limited institutional or commercial visi
 bility\, committed to professionalising their practice through research an
 d experimentation\, and open to dialogue and collective participation. HOW
  TO APPLY: one PDF (max 10 MB) with a description of your practice\, a res
 idency proposal\, an exhibition proposal\, CV and portfolio\, via the onli
 ne application form (Google Form linked from the call page). Deadline 28 O
 ctober 2026 at 23:59 CET.\n\nOrganisation: Cas-co\, Leuven and Kunsthal Me
 chelen\nLocation: Cas-co\, Leuven\, Belgium\, within the Off the Grid prog
 ramme\, with the closing group exhibition at Kunsthal Mechelen. Open only 
 to Belgium-based visual artists.\nAward: EUR 6\,080 total including VAT: a
 n artist fee of EUR 1\,100 per month\, a transportation allowance of EUR 1
 20 per month\, and a one-time production budget of EUR 1\,200. Kunsthal Me
 chelen provides additional artist and production fees for the exhibition. 
 No application fee.\nDuration: Four months\, 14 January to 14 May 2027\, f
 ollowed by a group exhibition at Kunsthal Mechelen from 4 June to 29 Augus
 t 2027\n\nMore: https://cas-co.be/nieuws/cas-coxkunsthalmechelen-artist-op
 en-call-deadline-28-10-26?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium
 =referral
URL:https://cas-co.be/nieuws/cas-coxkunsthalmechelen-artist-open-call-deadl
 ine-28-10-26?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Cas-co\, Leuven\, Belgium\, within the Off the Grid programme\, wi
 th the closing group exhibition at Kunsthal Mechelen. Open only to Belgium
 -based visual artists.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:transatlantic-stars-visual-arts-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261030
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261031
SUMMARY:Deadline: Transatlantic Stars Visual Arts Program 2027: US residenc
 ies for EU artists
DESCRIPTION:The EU Delegation to the United States invites mid-career and e
 stablished visual artists from the 27 EU Member States to apply for the Tr
 ansatlantic Stars Visual Arts Program 2027\, an eight-week artist-in-resid
 ence placement at one of six residency sites across the United States from
  April to early June 2027. Each artist is paired one-to-one with a local A
 merican collaborator to co-create work\, and must produce at least one phy
 sical artwork\; the programme concludes with a mandatory two-day summit in
  Washington\, D.C.\, where the resulting works are exhibited. All visual m
 ediums with a physical space component are accepted. SUPPORT: a living sti
 pend and a materials budget\, plus airfare\, visa assistance\, on-site lod
 ging\, studio space\, and access to host facilities\, equipment and commun
 ity networks. ELIGIBILITY: citizens of an EU Member State with a valid pas
 sport\; mid-career or established artists who meet at least four of five p
 rofessional standing criteria\; English proficiency\; availability for the
  full April to early June 2027 period. APPLICATIONS: via the Airtable form
  linked from the call page. DEADLINE: 30 October 2026 at 11:59 PM CET\, or
  earlier if the cap of 300 applications is reached first. Contact: arts@tr
 sproject.eu. Parallel Transatlantic Stars calls for film and music run on 
 the same deadline.\n\nOrganisation: European Union Delegation to the Unite
 d States\nLocation: Eight-week residencies at six host sites across the Un
 ited States\, April to early June 2027\, ending with a two-day summit in W
 ashington\, D.C. Open to citizens of EU Member States.\nAward: Fully funde
 d: each selected artist receives a living stipend and a materials budget (
 amounts not published)\, plus airfare\, visa assistance\, on-site lodging\
 , studio space and access to host facilities. Six placements. Free to appl
 y.\nDuration: Eight weeks\, April to early June 2027\, concluding with a m
 andatory two-day summit in Washington\, D.C.\n\nMore: https://www.eeas.eur
 opa.eu/delegations/united-states-america/transatlantic-rising-stars-projec
 t-visual-arts_en?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.eeas.europa.eu/delegations/united-states-america/transatlan
 tic-rising-stars-project-visual-arts_en?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Eight-week residencies at six host sites across the United States\
 , April to early June 2027\, ending with a two-day summit in Washington\, 
 D.C. Open to citizens of EU Member States.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:neue-baeckerei-bubble-open-call-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: BUBBLE Open Call 2026 at Neue Baeckerei (Wiesbaden)
DESCRIPTION:Neue Baeckerei in Wiesbaden invites artists worldwide to its se
 cond exhibition\, BUBBLE\, curated by Fee-Gloria Groenemeyer\, exploring t
 he bubbles we live in and whether they act as safe spaces or as boundaries
 . All media and forms of artistic practice are welcome\, and both existing
  and new works can be proposed\, regardless of location or experience leve
 l. SUPPORT: selected artists receive an artist fee of EUR 300 and up to EU
 R 100 towards shipping and insurance. EXHIBITION: opening 12 December 2026
 \, on view through 3 January 2027\; works must be available from 1 Decembe
 r 2026 to 9 January 2027. HOW TO APPLY: via the Google Form linked from th
 e open-call page\; no individual feedback is given to unsuccessful applica
 nts. No application fee. DEADLINE: 30 September 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Neu
 e Baeckerei\, Wiesbaden\nLocation: Neue Baeckerei\, Wiesbaden\, Germany. O
 pen to artists worldwide.\nAward: EUR 300 artist fee per selected artist\,
  plus up to EUR 100 towards shipping and insurance. No application fee.\nD
 uration: Exhibition opens 12 December 2026 and runs to 3 January 2027\; wo
 rks must be available from 1 December 2026 to 9 January 2027\n\nMore: http
 s://www.neuebaeckerei.com/open-call-en?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.neuebaeckerei.com/open-call-en?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Neue Baeckerei\, Wiesbaden\, Germany. Open to artists worldwide.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:schlossmediale-werdenberg-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261018
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261019
SUMMARY:Deadline: Schlossmediale Call for Art Residency 2027 (Schloss Werde
 nberg\, Switzerland)
DESCRIPTION:Schlossmediale\, the international festival of early music\, ne
 w music and audiovisual art at Werdenberg Castle in the canton of St. Gall
 en\, invites three solo artists to a five-week residency from 17 May to 27
  June 2027. The works developed on site are shown in the castle during the
  14th festival edition (17-26 June 2027). The 2027 theme is KLATSCH! (Rumo
 ur-Impact): sound and rumour\, applause and gossip\, oral tradition\, coll
 ective memory\, and the ways every era spreads its information. MEDIUMS: s
 ound art\, sound studies\, audiovisual art\, experimental instrument build
 ing\, visual art\, installation\, sculpture\, land art and performance\; s
 ound installations without a visual dimension are not considered. SUPPORT:
  CHF 4\,000 grant\, CHF 1\,000 for travel\, transport and meals\, up to CH
 F 1\,000 for materials\, and accommodation in a shared house in Werdenberg
  (individual rooms\, shared kitchen and living areas). ELIGIBILITY: solo a
 rtists with professional experience (no groups or duos) who can live and w
 ork on site for the full period and complete a finished\, functional work 
 by the festival opening\; residents present their work on castle tours and
  attend the whole festival. Working space at the castle is limited and no 
 studios are provided. HOW TO APPLY: exclusively online via the application
  portal linked from the open-call page. DEADLINE: 18 October 2026.\n\nOrga
 nisation: Schlossmediale Werdenberg\nLocation: Werdenberg Castle\, canton 
 of St. Gallen\, Switzerland. Open internationally to solo artists\; accomm
 odation in a shared house in Werdenberg.\nAward: CHF 4\,000 grant per resi
 dent\, plus CHF 1\,000 for travel\, transport and meals\, up to CHF 1\,000
  for material costs\, and accommodation in a shared house (individual room
 s). Three residencies awarded.\nDuration: Five-week residency from 17 May 
 to 27 June 2027\, with the 14th Schlossmediale festival on 17-26 June 2027
 \n\nMore: https://schlossmediale.ch/festival-schlossmediale/ausstellung/op
 en-call-2027-en?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://schlossmediale.ch/festival-schlossmediale/ausstellung/open-call
 -2027-en?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Werdenberg Castle\, canton of St. Gallen\, Switzerland. Open inter
 nationally to solo artists\; accommodation in a shared house in Werdenberg
 .
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:arts-convergences-video-prize-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261019
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261020
SUMMARY:Deadline: Arts Convergences Video Prize\, 6th edition (short films 
 on mental illness)
DESCRIPTION:The Arts Convergences Video Prize rewards very short films that
  raise public awareness of the lives of adults living with mental illness\
 , showing their difficulties but above all their talents and their ability
  to move us. Sixth edition\, run with Thanks for Nothing and supported by 
 the City of Paris\, Psycom\, the Centre Hospitalier de Plaisir and the Fal
 ret Foundation. FORMAT: 90 seconds to 4 minutes\, any genre (comedy\, thri
 ller\, documentary\, news report\, animation\, stills\, motion) and any ca
 mera. IMPORTANT EXCLUSIONS: the rules explicitly disallow artistic videos 
 of an experimental nature\, music videos\, advertisements\, institutional 
 films and prevention campaigns\, so frame the work as a narrative or docum
 entary short rather than video art. Videos in languages other than French 
 are disqualified without French subtitles\, and end credits must include a
  mandatory partnership mention. ELIGIBILITY: open to anyone over 18 who ho
 lds the rights to the video\; candidates produce the film at their own cos
 t. SELECTION: jury of professionals judges relevance to the theme first\, 
 then originality and creativity\, then technical quality\; 15 shortlisted 
 videos go to a public online vote about 3 weeks before the ceremony. Selec
 ted candidates transfer non-commercial worldwide rights for 10 years and t
 he organisers guarantee a public presentation of selected videos in a lead
 ing cultural institution at their cost. Deadline 19 October 2026\, midnigh
 t CET\, via the candidate space on the website. Awards ceremony 26 Novembe
 r 2026 at the Forum des Images\, Paris\, open to the public.\n\nOrganisati
 on: Arts Convergences\, in partnership with Thanks for Nothing\nLocation: 
 Open internationally\; organizer based in France. Submission is online\; w
 inners should attend or be represented at the awards ceremony in Paris (26
  November 2026\, Forum des Images). Videos not in French must carry French
  subtitles.\nAward: EUR 5\,000 total: Grand Prize EUR 2\,000\, Jury Prize 
 EUR 1\,500\, Public Choice Prize EUR 1\,500 (online vote). Additional priz
 es may be awarded. No entry fee.\nDuration: One-off prize for a finished v
 ery short film.\n\nMore: https://artsconvergences.com/prix-video/?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://artsconvergences.com/prix-video/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Open internationally\; organizer based in France. Submission is on
 line\; winners should attend or be represented at the awards ceremony in P
 aris (26 November 2026\, Forum des Images). Videos not in French must carr
 y French subtitles.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:culture-moves-europe-mobility-2026-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270430
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270501
SUMMARY:Deadline: Culture Moves Europe: Call for Individual Mobility 2026-2
 027
DESCRIPTION:Flagship EU mobility grant for artists and cultural professiona
 ls: individual or group (up to 5 people) mobility to carry out an artistic
  or cultural project in another Creative Europe country\, with the support
  of an international partner of your own choosing (an individual or an org
 anisation). The project must follow 2 of the 4 objectives: to learn\, to c
 reate\, to explore\, or to connect. SECTORS: architecture\, cultural herit
 age\, design and fashion design\, literature\, music\, performing arts\, a
 nd visual arts\; no specific level of experience required. ELIGIBILITY: ag
 ed 18+\, legally residing in one of the Creative Europe countries\, includ
 ing the overseas countries and territories and outermost regions (Netherla
 nds eligible). GRANT: EUR 85 daily allowance per day of project implementa
 tion\; travel allowance EUR 400 under 5\,000 km or EUR 800 from 5\,000 km 
 (distance calculated automatically in the application form as a one-way st
 raight line)\; top-ups for green mobility (EUR 400)\, OCT/outermost region
 s (EUR 175)\, family (EUR 200 per child under 18) and visa (EUR 120)\; acc
 essibility support of EUR 30 per day plus personal assistance or sign lang
 uage interpretation covered. APPLICATION: official national identification
 \, proof of legal residence\, short CV\, artistic and creative portfolio\,
  and a letter of invitation from the international partner. TIMELINE: call
  opened 1 October 2026\, 9:00 CEST\; deadline 30 April 2027\, 23:59 CEST.\
 n\nOrganisation: Creative Europe (Culture Moves Europe)\, implemented by t
 he Goethe-Institut\nLocation: Creative Europe countries (incl. overseas co
 untries and territories and outermost regions)\; the project takes place i
 n another Creative Europe country than your residence\nAward: EUR 85 per d
 ay of project implementation\, plus travel allowance of EUR 400 (under 5\,
 000 km) or EUR 800 (from 5\,000 km). Top-ups where applicable: green mobil
 ity EUR 400\, overseas countries and territories / outermost regions EUR 1
 75\, family EUR 200 per child under 18\, visa EUR 120. Accessibility suppo
 rt: EUR 30 per day plus actual cost or fixed allowance for personal assist
 ance or sign language interpretation. No application fee.\nDuration: Proje
 ct-based\n\nMore: https://culture.ec.europa.eu/culture-moves-europe/call-f
 or-individual-mobility?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=re
 ferral
URL:https://culture.ec.europa.eu/culture-moves-europe/call-for-individual-m
 obility?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Creative Europe countries (incl. overseas countries and territorie
 s and outermost regions)\; the project takes place in another Creative Eur
 ope country than your residence
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cnc-creation-immersive-2026-oct@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261012
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261013
SUMMARY:Deadline: CNC: Fonds d'aide a la creation immersive (October 2026 s
 ession)
DESCRIPTION:The CNC's flagship fund for immersive creation (successor to DI
 CReAM since 2022): VR\, mixed reality and interactive narrative works\, as
 sessed by a commission chaired by Jean-Michel Jarre. Four strands cover th
 e whole chain: writing (ecriture)\, preproduction\, production and portage
  (bringing a finished work to audiences). AMOUNTS: the aid page states per
 centage caps rather than fixed sums\; CNC's published results pages for 20
 25 show writing grants of EUR 10\,000 to 12\,000\, preproduction up to EUR
  60\,000 and production up to EUR 80\,000. ELIGIBILITY: individual authors
  who are French nationals or legal residents of an EU/EEA state\, so Nethe
 rlands-based authors qualify\; companies and associations must be establis
 hed in France\; the project must be conceived/written in French and at lea
 st 50% of expenses must be in France. The fund runs four sessions per year
 \; this session closes 12 October 2026 (commission December 2026).\n\nOrga
 nisation: CNC (Centre national du cinema et de l'image animee)\nLocation: 
