 plication round in 2026: the central fund and all 17 regional funds accept
  applications together from 15 to 30 October. It funds all fields of art a
 nd science\, with one-year and multi-year working grants as the cornerston
 e alongside project grants for individuals\, working groups and organisati
 ons. SCALE: around EUR 49 million awarded annually across roughly 2\,100 g
 rants (about 20\,600 applications in 2025\, including 165 multi-year grant
 s)\; recent October rounds averaged over 450 grants of one or more years\,
  and working grants can extend up to four years. ELIGIBILITY: Finnish nati
 onals and people or organisations residing or working in Finland\; other a
 pplicants qualify if the application demonstrates clear\, strong ties to F
 inland or Finnish culture. HOW: apply online during the window via the fou
 ndation's grant service. DEADLINE: 30 October 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Finni
 sh Cultural Foundation (Suomen Kulttuurirahasto)\nLocation: Finland. Open 
 to Finnish nationals\, people and organisations residing or working in Fin
 land\, and other applicants with demonstrable strong ties to Finland or Fi
 nnish culture.\nAward: Around EUR 49 million awarded annually across rough
 ly 2\,100 grants\; recent October rounds have averaged over 450 working an
 d project grants covering one or more years\, with working grants extendin
 g up to four years. No application fee.\nDuration: Working grants of one t
 o four years\; project grants per project\n\nMore: https://skr.fi/en/grant
 s/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
