DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270201
SUMMARY:Deadline: Kulturstiftung des Bundes: General Project Funding\, Janu
 ary 2027 round (Allgemeine Projektfoerderung)
DESCRIPTION:Winter round of Germany's flagship open\, non-thematic federal 
 project line\, one of the largest European funders that will back a festiv
 al\, exhibition programme or multi-partner convening run by an organisatio
 n rather than an individual artist. It funds large innovative projects acr
 oss all artistic fields\, explicitly including New Media alongside visual 
 and performing arts\, music\, film\, photography and architecture. There i
 s no published maximum\, but the EUR 50\,000 minimum total project cost se
 ts the scale\, and at least 20 percent co-financing is mandatory. This rou
 nd closes 31 January 2027 at 12:00 CET\, with decisions at the external ju
 ry meeting in May 2027\; no project may start before its jury date\, so pl
 an four to six months of lead time. Non-German organisations are genuinely
  eligible\, which is unusual at this scale\, provided the project is visib
 le in Germany and has an international dimension. Two practical barriers: 
 the application form must be completed in German\, and project communicati
 ons must include a German-language version.\n\nOrganisation: Kulturstiftun
 g des Bundes (German Federal Cultural Foundation)\nLocation: Activity must
  be visible to audiences in Germany. Institutions headquartered in Germany
  or abroad may apply.\nAward: No fixed ceiling\, but total project costs m
 ust exceed EUR 50\,000 to be eligible. The Foundation allocates up to EUR 
 10 million per year across this line. At least 20 percent of total project
  costs must be secured from own capital and/or third-party funding. No app
 lication fee.\nDuration: Project-length. Projects may not begin before the
  jury meeting.\n\nMore: https://www.kulturstiftung-des-bundes.de/en/themes
 _focuses/general_project_funding.html?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.kulturstiftung-des-bundes.de/en/themes_focuses/general_proj
 ect_funding.html?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Activity must be visible to audiences in Germany. Institutions hea
 dquartered in Germany or abroad may apply.
END:VEVENT
