 and visual artists connected to Ireland. AWARDS: EUR 10\,000 each to two w
 inners\, one in Visual Art and one in Craft + Applied Art (total fund usua
 lly around EUR 30\,000)\; shortlisted artists also receive a smaller finan
 cial award\, amount to be confirmed. ELIGIBILITY: craft and visual artists
  living and working on the island of Ireland\, and Irish-born artists work
 ing overseas\; any career stage with demonstrated artistic merit\; full-ti
 me students are normally not considered\; previous main-award winners cann
 ot reapply. APPLICATION: online\, no fee. TIMELINE: applications open 12:0
 0 noon on 16 October 2026. DEADLINE: 11 December 2026\, 17:00.\n\nOrganisa
 tion: The Golden Fleece Award (Lillias Mitchell Trust)\nLocation: Island o
 f Ireland (artists living and working in Ireland or Northern Ireland)\, pl
 us Irish-born artists working overseas.\nAward: EUR 10\,000 each for two c
 ategory winners (Visual Art\, and Craft + Applied Art)\; total fund usuall
 y around EUR 30\,000\, with shortlisted artists also receiving a smaller f
 inancial award (amount to be confirmed). No application fee.\nDuration: An
