DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261023
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261024
SUMMARY:Deadline: CreArt 3.0: Artist Residency in Lublin 2026
DESCRIPTION:The City of Lublin and Warsztaty Kultury host a 17-day CreArt 3
 .0 residency for two artists (one from Lublin\, one from another CreArt ne
 twork city) who develop a joint project based on a 1.5-metre movable globe
  originally made for the Planet Lublin installation\, to be presented in L
 ublin's public space. WHAT YOU GET: EUR 800 gross grant per artist (paid w
 ithin 21 days after the residency\; 20 percent income tax reduction for ar
 tists from abroad)\, up to EUR 460 gross production budget\, and\, for art
 ists from CreArt cities\, flights to Warsaw or Lublin\, accommodation and 
 two meals a day (Warsaw to Lublin transfer at the artist's own cost). ELIG
 IBILITY: individual artists (no groups) born or residing in a CreArt netwo
 rk city\, HDLU members\, or Ukrainian artists via the Lviv Artistic Counci
 l Dialogue\; an arts degree or equivalent documented track record is requi
 red\; no age limit\; a European Health Insurance Card or equivalent is req
 uired. Application: one English PDF (ID\, proof of network-city connection
 \, CV\, portfolio\, project proposal) via the CreArt website. Results by 3
 0 October 2026. An English final report of at least 6 pages is due afterwa
 rds. DEADLINE: 23 October 2026.\n\nOrganisation: City of Lublin and Warszt
 aty Kultury (CreArt network)\nLocation: Lublin\, Poland. Open to artists b
 orn or residing in a CreArt network city (Kaunas\, Liepaja\, Skopje\, Avei
 ro\, Valladolid\, Lublin\, Venice\, Clermont-Ferrand\, Rouen\, Regensburg\
 , Ceske Budejovice\, Oulu)\, plus HDLU members (Croatia) and Ukrainian art
 ists via the Lviv Artistic Council Dialogue.\nAward: EUR 800 gross grant p
 er artist plus up to EUR 460 gross for materials and production\; flights\
 , accommodation and two meals a day covered for artists from CreArt networ
 k cities. No application fee.\nDuration: 17-day residency\, 12 to 28 Novem
 ber 2026\, with a public presentation in Lublin on 27 November.\n\nMore: h
 ttps://creart2-eu.org/open-calls/open-call-creart-3-0-artist-residency-pro
 gram-in-lublin-2026?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=refer
 ral
URL:https://creart2-eu.org/open-calls/open-call-creart-3-0-artist-residency
 -program-in-lublin-2026?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=r
 eferral
LOCATION:Lublin\, Poland. Open to artists born or residing in a CreArt netw
 ork city (Kaunas\, Liepaja\, Skopje\, Aveiro\, Valladolid\, Lublin\, Venic
 e\, Clermont-Ferrand\, Rouen\, Regensburg\, Ceske Budejovice\, Oulu)\, plu
 s HDLU members (Croatia) and Ukrainian artists via the Lviv Artistic Counc
