SUMMARY:Deadline: Dance Ireland Residencies\, Spring/Summer 2027 (DanceHous
 e Dublin\, EUR 750 per week)
DESCRIPTION:Dance Ireland's residency programme at DanceHouse\, Dublin\, gi
 ves dance artists paid studio time to develop ideas for a new work\, carry
  out artistic research or maintain a studio practice. It is aimed at artis
 ts and projects that are not otherwise funded. WHAT YOU GET: EUR 750 per w
 eek for the participating artist\, subsidised studio space\, an additional
  EUR 750 distance bursary for artists based more than 100 km from Dublin\,
  and one dedicated Disabled Dance Artist residency with a EUR 750 bursary 
 and access budget. ELIGIBILITY: Professional Members of Dance Ireland for 
 the general residencies (allow at least a week to renew membership before 
 the deadline)\; the Disabled Dance Artist residency does not require membe
 rship but is for Irish or Ireland-based artists. APPLICATION: read the gui
 delines PDF\, then complete the Google Form linked from the opportunity pa
 ge\; late applications are not accepted. DEADLINE: Monday 9 November 2026 
 at 12 noon.\n\nOrganisation: Dance Ireland\nLocation: Dublin\, Ireland (Da
 nceHouse). For Professional Members of Dance Ireland\; the Disabled Dance 
 Artist residency is open to Irish or Ireland-based artists without members
 hip.\nAward: EUR 750 per week stipend plus subsidised studio space. An ext
 ra EUR 750 bursary for artists living more than 100 km from Dublin (accomm
 odation or travel). One Disabled Dance Artist residency with a EUR 750 bur
 sary and an access budget. No application fee.\nDuration: Week-long reside
 ncies (Monday to Friday) between January and July 2027\; listed Studio 6 w
 eeks run 25 January to 14 May 2027\, other weeks can be proposed.\n\nMore:
  https://www.danceireland.ie/whats-on/opportunities/ss-2027-dance-ireland-
 residencies/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.danceireland.ie/whats-on/opportunities/ss-2027-dance-irelan
 d-residencies/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Dublin\, Ireland (DanceHouse). For Professional Members of Dance I
 reland\; the Disabled Dance Artist residency is open to Irish or Ireland-b
 ased artists without membership.
