UID:alpaca-festival-2027-open-call@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Deadline: Alpaca Festival 2027: Open Call for Pattern-Based Perform
 ances\, Workshops and Talks (Sheffield\, UK)
DESCRIPTION:Alpaca is a festival and conference on algorithmic patterns in 
 the creative arts\, run by the non-profit Pattern Club in Sheffield. It br
 ings together live coders\, weavers\, braiders\, origami makers\, musician
 s and other practitioners who make patterns by procedure\, and it welcomes
  contemporary algorithmic art that is human-authored. THEME (talks): makin
 g languages and notations for making patterns\, with unexpected interpreta
 tions welcome. WHAT YOU CAN PROPOSE: live performances\, hands-on workshop
 s\, and roughly 20-minute conference talks\; accepted abstracts (max two p
 ages) are published open access with a DOI and may be invited into an edit
 ed volume. WHAT YOU GET: performers receive an artist fee plus national tr
 avel\; workshop leaders receive an artist fee\, materials and national tra
 vel. The organisers state they cannot confirm fee amounts at this stage an
 d may cover extra costs on request\; international travel is not covered a
 part from a small European train budget. Talks are unpaid: in-person speak
 ers get a free festival pass and lunch on the conference days. EXCLUSIONS:
  submissions focused on generative AI or unsupervised pattern generation b
 y LLMs. APPLICATION: via the online form at calls.alpaca.cc\; questions to
  contact@alpaca.cc. DEADLINE: 1 November 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Pattern Cl
 ub (Alpaca Festival)\nLocation: Sheffield\, UK\, with some talks and activ
 ities online. Open internationally\, but only national (UK) travel is cove
 red\, plus a small budget for European train travel.\nAward: Performances:
  artist fee plus national travel expenses. Workshops: artist fee\, materia
 ls expenses and national travel expenses. Fee amounts are not yet confirme
 d (tight budget)\; additional costs may be covered on request. Internation
 al travel is not covered beyond a small European train budget. Conference 
 talks: no fee or expenses\, in-person speakers get a free festival weekend
  pass and lunch on 6 and 7 May. No application fee.\nDuration: Festival 6 
 to 9 May 2027: conference talks 6 and 7 May\, workshops and performances 7
  to 9 May. Decisions expected December 2026.\n\nMore: https://alpaca.cc/ca
 ll/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://alpaca.cc/call/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_mediu
 m=referral
LOCATION:Sheffield\, UK\, with some talks and activities online. Open inter
 nationally\, but only national (UK) travel is covered\, plus a small budge
 t for European train travel.
END:VEVENT
