DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270131
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270201
SUMMARY:Deadline: Berlin Senate: Zweijaehrige Basisfoerderung 2028-2029 for
  performing arts and dance groups and individual artists
DESCRIPTION:The Basisfoerderung is Berlin's two-year structural line for th
 e independent performing arts scene\, giving groups and solo artists witho
 ut a production venue planning security beyond single projects. WHO: profe
 ssional\, privately organised groups and individual artists in dance\, per
 forming and performative arts (all genres) with their main working base in
  Berlin\, a visible public presence in the Berlin scene and a demonstrated
  artistic identity\; a group should show at least two years of continuous\
 , independent work in the applying line-up. Legal entities and natural per
 sons can apply. CONDITIONS: at least one new production in Berlin per fund
 ing year (revivals only in exceptional cases)\; if performance costs are r
 equested\, box-office income must appear in the financing plan. WHAT IT FU
 NDS: production-related personnel and material costs\, Berlin performance 
 costs\, general costs for developing and securing working structures\, and
  costs for accessible production. Jury criteria include continuity and dev
 elopment of previous work\, a convincing longer-term artistic perspective\
 , quality of the planned productions\, own and third-party income\, networ
 king and relevance to Berlin's cultural infrastructure. APPLICATION: onlin
 e via the Berlin funding portal (fms.verwalt-berlin.de) with the official 
 two-year financing plan\; the 2028-2029 Infoblatt is published in December
  2026\, the current sheet covers 2026-27. ACCESS (Performing Arts Programm
  Berlin) helps with online applications. DEADLINE: 31 January 2027\, 24:00
  (cut-off deadline\, no late submissions).\n\nOrganisation: Berlin Senate 
 Department for Culture and Social Cohesion\nLocation: Berlin\, Germany. Fo
 r professional groups (privately organised) and individual artists in danc
 e\, performing and performative arts without their own venue\, with their 
 main working base in Berlin.\nAward: Two-year project funding (2028 and 20
 29) covering production-related personnel and material costs\, Berlin perf
 ormance costs and certain general costs for developing and securing workin
 g structures. No published minimum or maximum\; the amount follows the fin
 ancing plan you submit\, and only part of the running costs is co-financed
 . Fees in the plan should follow the Berlin minimum-fee recommendations. N
 o application fee.\nDuration: Calendar years 2028 and 2029. Call published
  in December of the year before the deadline\; funding starts January 2028
 .\n\nMore: https://www.berlin.de/sen/kultur/foerderung/foerderprogramme/da
 rstellende-kuenste-tanz/artikel.81996.php?utm_source=artificialnouveaugran
 tdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.berlin.de/sen/kultur/foerderung/foerderprogramme/darstellen
 de-kuenste-tanz/artikel.81996.php?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&ut
 m_medium=referral
LOCATION:Berlin\, Germany. For professional groups (privately organised) an
 d individual artists in dance\, performing and performative arts without t
 heir own venue\, with their main working base in Berlin.
END:VEVENT
