SUMMARY:Deadline: Berlin Senate: Vierjaehrige Konzeptfoerderung 2028-2031 f
 or performing arts and dance groups and individual artists
DESCRIPTION:The Konzeptfoerderung is the longest structural funding line Be
 rlin offers independent performing arts groups and individual artists who 
 have no venue of their own: four years of funding for an artistic concept 
 rather than single productions. WHO: professional\, privately organised gr
 oups and individual artists in dance\, performing and performative arts (a
 ll genres) whose work has shown a distinct artistic character over several
  years\, has met with interest from audiences and critics\, and who have t
 heir main working base in Berlin. CONDITIONS: at least one new production 
 in Berlin per funding year\; revivals only in exceptional cases. WHAT IT F
 UNDS: production-related personnel and material costs\, performance costs\
 , and general costs needed to develop and secure the artistic work that ca
 nnot be assigned to individual productions. APPLICATION: online via the Be
 rlin funding portal (fms.verwalt-berlin.de) with the official four-year sa
 mple financing plan\; read the Konzeptfoerderung information sheet and the
  minimum-fee recommendations first. The 2028-2031 call documents are publi
 shed in December 2026. ACCESS (Performing Arts Programm Berlin) offers hel
 p with online applications. DEADLINE: 31 January 2027 (end of day\; cut-of
 f deadline).\n\nOrganisation: Berlin Senate Department for Culture and Soc
 ial Cohesion\nLocation: Berlin\, Germany. For professional groups (private
 ly organised) and individual artists in dance\, performing and performativ
 e arts without their own venue\, with their main working base in Berlin.\n
 Award: Four-year funding (2028 to 2031) covering production-related person
 nel and material costs\, performance costs and general costs for developin
 g and securing the artistic work. No published minimum or maximum\; the am
 ount follows the four-year financing plan you submit. Fees should follow t
 he Berlin minimum-fee recommendations. No application fee.\nDuration: Four
  calendar years\, 2028 to 2031. The programme is advertised every fourth y
 ear in December for the four years after next\; funding starts January 202
 8.\n\nMore: https://www.berlin.de/sen/kultur/foerderung/foerderprogramme/d
 arstellende-kuenste-tanz/artikel.1033731.php?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.berlin.de/sen/kultur/foerderung/foerderprogramme/darstellen
 de-kuenste-tanz/artikel.1033731.php?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Berlin\, Germany. For professional groups (privately organised) an
 d individual artists in dance\, performing and performative arts without t
 heir own venue\, with their main working base in Berlin.
