UID:dm-award-connecting-worlds-karlsruhe-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T162048Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261125
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261126
SUMMARY:Deadline: dm-Award connecting worlds 2027: PLAYGROUND (projection m
 apping and public-space media art\, EUR 10\,000 prize plus up to EUR 20\,0
 00 production\, SCHLOSSLICHTSPIELE Karlsruhe)
DESCRIPTION:The UNESCO City of Media Arts Office of Karlsruhe's Department 
 of Cultural Affairs awards the dm-Award connecting worlds\, with dm-droger
 ie markt as awarding partner\, ZKM | Center for Art and Media Karlsruhe as
  curatorial partner and KME as organiser of the SCHLOSSLICHTSPIELE Light F
 estival. Under the motto PLAYGROUND\, the call seeks projects that connect
  the digital space of the projection mappings on Karlsruhe Palace's facade
  with the analogue space of the Market Square\, playfully activating publi
 c space. FORMAT: every project must have two elements: a projection mappin
 g on the palace facade (2 to 5 minutes) and at least one satellite on the 
 Market Square that also works independently of the projection and is publi
 cly and freely accessible. Examples include interactive projections and ga
 me elements with audience participation\, installations or media artworks 
 relating to the projection\, combinations of performance\, concerts or act
 ions with projection mapping\, sculptural\, 3D or immersive formats\, new 
 technologies\, and collaborations between local and international players.
  The winner is realised in 2027 during the SCHLOSSLICHTSPIELE and the exhi
 bition Media art is here\, running four weeks between mid-August and mid-S
 eptember 2027. WHO: artists worldwide\, individually or as a collective. W
 HAT YOU GET: a EUR 10\,000 prize\, up to EUR 20\,000 net production fundin
 g (which must cover all production costs\, including fees\, equipment and 
 the winners' travel)\, plus curatorial and technical support\; technical r
 equirements are set out in the Production Guidelines. APPLICATION: via the
  call page\; questions to cityofmediaarts@kultur.karlsruhe.de. Application
  period 9 October to 25 November 2026\, closing at 13:00 CET.\n\nOrganisat
 ion: Karlsruhe UNESCO City of Media Arts Office (Cultural Office)\, with d
 m-drogerie markt\, ZKM | Center for Art and Media Karlsruhe and KME Karlsr
 uhe Marketing und Event\nLocation: Karlsruhe\, Germany (palace facade and 
 Market Square). Open internationally to individual artists and collectives
 .\nAward: EUR 10\,000 prize plus up to EUR 20\,000 net production funding 
 for the winning project (covering fees\, technical equipment and travel)\,
  with curatorial and technical support from the Cultural Office\, KME and 
 ZKM.\nDuration: Presented for 4 weeks between mid-August and mid-September
  2027 during the SCHLOSSLICHTSPIELE Light Festival and the exhibition Medi
 a art is here.\n\nMore: https://www.cityofmediaarts.de/en/events/apply-now
 -open-call-dm-award-connecting-worlds/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
